{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DoQFqYKU4afn3LnZtJ21BP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted experimental results for all planned experiments in the experiment_plan, under the \"best\" tier scenario. Let me carefully go through each planned experiment and generate realistic predicted results with rationales.\n\nLet me first understand the \"best\" tier:\n- SDGD-zero R2 fixes work, F1 significantly better than single-pass\n- Multi-model/multi-task full replication\n- All 3 claims hold\n- Key metric ranges given\n\nLet me go through each planned experiment:\n\n1. **exp-004** (MAVEN) - status: planned (but there's also a registry entry for exp004_maven_bcs that's DONE with conclusion: negative, and exp-004 DONE with success showing SCS stats). \n\nLooking at the registry more carefully, exp-004 has some batch-level results already completed, but the planned version still needs the full pairwise and per-type analysis. Let me focus on what's actually marked as planned in the experiment_plan and generate predictions for those remaining analyses. 个 planned 实验展开详细数据\". So I need to focus on experiments with status: planned.\n\nPlanned experiments:\n- exp-004 (MAVEN confusability study) - status: planned\n- exp-005 (DocRED) - status: planned\n- exp-006 (Interaction 2x2) - status: planned\n- exp-007 (Error taxonomy) - status: planned\n- exp-012 (Multi-model LLaMA) - status: planned\n- exp-008 (SDGD-zero Few-NERD) - status: planned\n- exp-009 (SDGD-zero MAVEN) - status: planned\n- exp-010 (SDGD-cal Few-NERD) - status: planned\n- exp-011 (SDGD-cal MAVEN) - status: planned\n- exp-013 (Random batching ablation) - status: planned\n- exp-014 (Per-type splitting) - status: planned\n- exp-015 (SCS validation) - status: planned\n\nI notice exp-008 shows as done/failed in the registry while R2 is running, but since the user asked about planned experiments I'll treat it as planned. Now I'm looking at the expected metric ranges for the \"best\" tier predictions, including the F1 deltas against baseline approaches and the statistical significance thresholds for the LLaMA experiments.\n\nNow I'm working through realistic predictions for each experiment, starting with exp-004 where I already have batch-level data showing higher batch centrality scores correlate with higher relaxed F1 scores, which actually contradicts the initial hypothesis at the batch level. The MAVEN pairwise correlation from the paper is already established at r=0.120 with p≈0, and the per-type analysis shows a positive direction suggesting a centrality confound effect.\n\nFor the remaining experiments, I'm mapping out expected outcomes: DocRED with its 96 relation types should show a strong pairwise signal, the 2x2 interaction test should confirm an additive model with slight super-additivity, the error taxonomy analysis should reveal clear differential patterns across error types, and the LLaMA multi-model comparison should yield correlations in the 0.1-0.2 range with p < 0.005. For the Few-NERD zero-shot experiments, the first run failed but the second should succeed with delta F1 improvements between 3-8 points, and I'm still working through the MAVEN zero-shot variant.\n\nNow I'm compiling the baseline numbers and preparing to structure everything in YAML with precise metrics, starting with the Few-NERD single-pass baseline at F1 = 0.414. I need to pick solid values within the predicted ranges for the best tier results. Looking at MAVEN, the baseline relaxed F1 at count_64 was 0.245, and SDGD should improve from there. I also notice exp-004 is marked as planned in the experiment plan even though there's some preliminary registry data, so I should include predictions for it—the MiniLM pairwise signal looks strong based on what's already been established. Now I'll draft the full YAML output.\n\nFor exp-004 specifically, I need to be careful about what's already known versus what's predicted. The paper already cites MAVEN MiniLM pairwise r=0.120, so the planned work is really the full count curve and within-count BCS correlation using the v2 prompt on a larger sample. I'll structure each experiment prediction with name, plan_id, description, expected results with detailed metrics, rationale, tables, figures, and analysis—making sure everything stays internally consistent with the best tier definition and existing data.\n\nFor SDGD-zero R2, the previous run failed due to implementation issues with the threshold and merge strategy. The fix adjusts both of those, and I'm expecting F1 to land around 0.469—that's roughly +5.5 percentage points over the baseline single-pass F1 of 0.414, which fits comfortably in the [3, 8] pp range for best tier. The random batching control should show F1 around 0.437, demonstrating that confusability-aware decomposition adds about 3 pp on top of the basic decomposition benefit.\n\nFor LLaMA, the pairwise correlation is around 0.14 with p < 1e-8, both well within expected ranges. Now I'm moving forward with writing out the full experimental plan, starting with exp-004 on the MAVEN dataset using the v2 prompt across 500 samples, establishing the pairwise correlations for MiniLM and Qwen3.\n\nFor exp-005 on DocRED with its 96 relation types at document level, I expect the pairwise signal to show significance. Then exp-006 tests the 2x2 factorial interaction between count and BCS, where I'm predicting an additive model with slight super-additivity at high-high values. In exp-007, I'm looking at systematic false positive classification across BCS bins, expecting type substitution errors to dominate in high-BCS regions while false negatives cluster in high-count bins. Finally, exp-008 covers the SDGD-zero Few-NERD setup.\n\nMoving through the remaining experiments: exp-009 applies SDGD-zero to MAVEN's 168 event types with relaxed F1 improvements, while exp-010 introduces empirical confusability calibration that marginally outperforms the zero-shot version. Exp-011 provides the full comparison table, and exp-012 replicates the pairwise correlation analysis with LLaMA-3.3-70B, yielding r ≈ 0.14. I'm also testing a random batching ablation in exp-013 where F1 falls between single-pass and SDGD performance, contrasting with exp-014's per-type splitting approach that achieves the best F1 but at 8x latency cost. Finally, exp-015 validates the SCS method against empirical confusion rankings, showing strong Spearman correlation.\n\nNow I'm moving into writing out the detailed YAML structure.\n\nI need to restructure figures_description and tables as arrays and include the actual table data. Let me work through the numbers more carefully for exp-008: the single-pass baseline on Few-NERD's 66 types achieves F1=0.414 with P=0.648 and R=0.304, while SDGD-zero partitions these into roughly 8 batches of 8 types each using confusability-minimizing grouping. This should yield F1≈0.470 with P=0.580 and R=0.392, where the recall gain of 8.8 percentage points comes from reduced attention dilution in smaller batches, though precision drops slightly.\n\nFor exp-013 with random batching at the same k=8 configuration, I'm seeing F1=0.445 with P=0.570 and R=0.365—the approach captures the count reduction benefit but misses the confusability optimization since random composition creates some high-similarity batches. The per-type splitting experiment (exp-014) with k=66 single-type batches reaches F1=0.478 with P=0.520 and R=0.442, representing the theoretical maximum.\n\nNow looking at the per-type results more closely: it maximizes recall by eliminating cross-type interference entirely, but precision suffers from losing that disambiguating context across types. The tradeoff is steep—66 API calls versus SDGD's 8—so the modest F1 gain doesn't justify the computational cost.\n\nSwitching to the LLaMA experiments, the pairwise correlation is much weaker at r=0.138 with p=2.1e-9, and per-type shows a negative correlation of ρ=-0.265 (p=0.038). The confusion ratio is extreme at 12x, which aligns with what I saw in Qwen3 but with a slightly lower effect magnitude, suggesting different models have varying sensitivity to confusability patterns.\n\nFor the MAVEN full dataset with v2 prompt on 500 samples, I'm examining the count curve using relaxed F1 metrics, and the pairwise MiniLM correlation comes in at r=0.120, confirming the pattern holds at scale.\n\nThe per-type direction is positive when accounting for the centrality confound, though the confusion rate ratio remains extreme at 8-12x—lower than Few-NERD because the schema is more homogeneous. In the SDGD-zero variant on MAVEN's 168 types split across ~14 batches, the baseline relaxed F1 at count_64 is 0.245, and SDGD-zero pushes it to 0.290, a gain of 4.5 percentage points over random's 2.8pp improvement.\n\nFor DocRED with 96 relation types at the document level, the pairwise correlation is r≈0.11 (p<0.001) and per-type shows ρ≈-0.22 (p≈0.04), with cross-task effects beginning to emerge between NER and RE.\n\nLooking at the tier requirements more carefully, the \"best\" tier specifies cross_task_significant_pairwise: [3, 3], meaning exactly 3 tasks are needed—Few-NERD for NER, FewRel for RE, and MAVEN for ED. DocRED would be a fourth task that strengthens the claim but isn't strictly required for the best tier designation.\n\nNow examining the 2x2 interaction effects with low counts...\n\nI'm seeing the performance metrics broken down by count and BCS levels, with F1 scores ranging from 0.18 to 0.38. The main effects show count and BCS both negatively impact performance, while their interaction is minimal. The ANOVA confirms count and BCS are statistically significant, but the interaction isn't. Then looking at the error taxonomy across BCS quartiles, I notice low BCS models struggle primarily with false negatives at 60%, while high BCS models distribute errors more evenly across substitution, boundary, and false negative categories.\n\nNow examining calibration experiments—using empirical confusion matrices from just 5-10 examples improves F1 by about 1.2 percentage points on both Few-NERD and MAVEN datasets compared to zero-shot approaches, suggesting that actual confusability patterns matter more than embedding-based proxies. The validation work shows embedding-based similarity correlates with empirical confusion at a moderate level around 0.42 Spearman correlation.\n\nI'm noticing the FewRel formal study is referenced as a requirement but doesn't appear as a distinct experiment in the plan—just the pilot is marked complete. Need to clarify whether this is meant to be a separate validation or if it's already covered elsewhere.\n\nNow I'm working through the baseline selection for Few-NERD SDGD-zero. The key tension is between using the full schema baseline (F1=0.414) versus a batch-sized baseline (F1=0.306), but SDGD's confusability-minimized batches should perform differently than random ones. The advantage comes from smaller batches reducing attention dilution and low-confusability batches reducing type substitution errors, though the merge step needs to handle overlapping spans carefully.\n\nR1 likely failed because the confusability threshold was miscalibrated or the merge strategy didn't handle conflicts well, but R2 should fix these issues and show F1 improvement over the single-pass approach. For the output, I'll keep the YAML clean and self-contained, focusing only on the planned experiments as specified—so exp-004 through exp-007 and beyond.\n\nLooking at the status breakdown, I count 12 planned experiments total that need predictions. I'm also wondering about the FewRel formal study mentioned in the key assumptions—it's supposed to confirm the pilot results showing a ≥15pp accuracy gap across extreme batch sizes, but I don't see it as a separate experiment ID in the plan. It might be embedded in exp-005 or unlisted, so I'll stick with what's explicitly documented.\n\nFor exp-004 specifically, the registry shows some MAVEN work is already complete with pairwise stats and batch-level results, but since the plan marks it as \"planned,\" I'll predict the full scope of results as if running the complete experiment end-to-end.\n\nNow I'll generate the final YAML with thorough predictions for each experiment.\n\nLooking at the SDGD performance deltas, the \"best\" tier estimates suggest single-pass F1 around 0.414, with SDGD-zero improving that by 3-8 percentage points to roughly 0.444-0.494. I'll estimate +5.5pp for Few-NERD, putting SDGD-zero at 0.469, then work backward from the random batching delta to calibrate those relative performance gaps.\n\nNow I'm thinking through how random batching with the same batch size would perform—it gets the benefit of smaller prompts reducing attention dilution, but without the confusability reduction that SDGD's strategic grouping provides. So random batching should land somewhere between single-pass and SDGD-zero, probably around 0.436 based on the delta ranges.\n\nThe real gains come from SDGD's confusability-aware separation, which prevents type substitution errors and adds another 3.3 percentage points on top of the random batching baseline. That puts the total improvement from single-pass to SDGD at 5.5 percentage points, which fits nicely within the expected bounds.\n\nGoing further with per-type splitting—one type per batch—maximizes decomposition and gets close to 0.480, but at the cost of losing cross-type context and requiring 8x more API calls, which hurts precision.\n\nWriting the YAML output... I'm noticing something counterintuitive here—in MAVEN, F1 actually improves as we include more event types (going from 0.106 at count_1 to 0.245 at count_64), which is the opposite pattern from Few-NERD. This happens because MAVEN's types are more homogeneous and additional types provide better context. So the full schema with all 168 types would likely reach around 0.26-0.28. That means SDGD, which reduces batch size, could theoretically hurt performance—but the confusability reduction within smaller batches should offset this and still provide a net benefit, especially in the best-tier scenarios where type specification quality matters most.\n\nFor MAVEN specifically, I should be more conservative with the improvement estimate since the relaxed F1 gains from larger type counts are driven by schema context rather than the confusability reduction that SDGD targets. I'll set the MAVEN SDGD improvement at +3 percentage points for relaxed F1 (compared to +5.5pp on Few-NERD), which is still meaningful but reflects that the mechanism works differently here. Using the count_64 baseline of 0.245 as my single-pass reference, SDGD-zero would reach approximately 0.275.\n\nNow I'm calibrating the random baseline and the delta between SDGD and random to stay within reasonable bounds—aiming for SDGD to outperform random by about 2.2 percentage points, which fits the expected range. Since MAVEN operates under different conditions than Few-NERD, I don't need to force its results into the same metric ranges; I can let them vary naturally while staying internally consistent.\n\nFor the DocRED experiment, I'm noting that document-level relation extraction is fundamentally different from sentence-level work—the longer context might actually reduce confusion between relation types, so I'll set the confusability signal at the lower end of what's plausible. For the LLaMA results, I'm pulling specific values from the \"best\" tier definition: a pairwise correlation around 0.138, a p-value near 3.2e-9, and confirmation that both Qwen3 and LLaMA show significant pairwise effects on Few-NERD. With all the numbers in place, I'm ready to write out the YAML configuration, keeping in mind that the narrative should emphasize the dual contribution of analysis and method, positioning this for EMNLP Main.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17638,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17638},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b7ad92b-97f6-47f3-a0ef-2ecf2be282d0","uuid":"507a0ce5-a2b8-49b3-90b0-b4ae359dcc71"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DoQFqYKU4afn3LnZtJ21BP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 framing 完全成立。三条 claim 无需调整：pairwise confusability 跨 3 任务 2 模型独立预测退化，\n  multi-channel 模型有 error taxonomy 支撑，SDGD-zero R2 修复后在 Few-NERD 和 MAVEN 上均显著优于 single-pass 和 random batching。\n  论文标题保持 \"analysis + method\" 双贡献定位。\n  Headline: \"Pairwise confusability predicts degradation (r=0.12–0.16) and SDGD yields +5.5 F1 on complex schemas.\"\n  EMNLP Main 无需降级。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-004: MAVEN 全量 confusability 研究\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"MAVEN Confusability Study (full)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      在 MAVEN 168 event types 上运行 v2 prompt，500 sample，完成 count curve、\n      batch-level BCS 对照、pairwise SCS→confusion 相关、per-type 分析及 centrality confound 量化。\n    expected_results:\n      count_curve_relaxed_f1:\n        count_1: 0.118\n        count_6: 0.142\n        count_12: 0.178\n        count_22: 0.210\n        count_44: 0.248\n        count_64: 0.261\n        count_168: 0.272\n      count_curve_exact_f1:\n        count_1: 0.011\n        count_6: 0.005\n        count_12: 0.010\n        count_22: 0.015\n        count_44: 0.020\n        count_64: 0.016\n        count_168: 0.014\n      pairwise_miniLM:\n        n_pairs: 14028\n        pearson_r: 0.120\n        pearson_p: 1.2e-45\n        spearman_rho: 0.135\n        spearman_p: 3.8e-58\n        nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.191\n        nonzero_spearman_p: 4.7e-4\n      pairwise_qwen3:\n        pearson_r: -0.007\n        pearson_p: 0.41\n        verdict: \"NOT_SIGNIFICANT — Qwen3 embeddings 无法在同质 schema 上捕获 pairwise signal\"\n      per_type_miniLM:\n        n_types: 148\n        filter: \"freq>=10\"\n        spearman_rho: 0.208\n        spearman_p: 0.011\n        direction: positive\n        verdict: \"CENTRALITY CONFOUND — 方向与假设相反\"\n      per_type_qwen3:\n        spearman_rho: 0.189\n        spearman_p: 0.021\n        direction: positive\n        verdict: \"CENTRALITY CONFOUND — 两种 embedding 方向一致，排除 embedding 压缩假说\"\n      centrality_analysis:\n        mean_bcs_vs_type_frequency_r: 0.34\n        mean_bcs_vs_type_frequency_p: 2.1e-5\n        interpretation: \"高 mean BCS = 语义中心类型 = 高频/LLM 更熟悉 = 更高 F1\"\n      batch_level_extreme:\n        count_6_high_bcs_relaxed_f1: 0.218\n        count_6_low_bcs_relaxed_f1: 0.098\n        count_12_high_bcs_relaxed_f1: 0.192\n        count_12_low_bcs_relaxed_f1: 0.114\n        confusion_rate_ratio_extreme_count6: 8.2\n        confusion_rate_ratio_extreme_count12: 6.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 168 个 event types 来自同一语义域（FrameNet 层级结构），SCS 分布高度集中\n      （mean=0.216, std=0.103），不像 Few-NERD 有跨域分离。\n      Pairwise MiniLM 信号成立（r=0.120）因为 MiniLM 的通用语义空间在细粒度事件类型间保留了足够区分度，\n      而 Qwen3 指令调优后的表征空间过度压缩了语义邻近类型。\n      Per-type 正方向是 centrality confound 的典型表现：在同质 schema 中，\n      mean BCS 高的类型恰好是语义网络的中心节点（如 \"Attack\", \"Meeting\"），\n      这些类型在训练语料中高频出现，LLM 先验知识更强，F1 自然更高。\n      这不是假设失败，而是方法论贡献——揭示了 per-type 聚合何时失效。\n      Batch-level 极端组对照仍然显示 high-BCS 组更高（与 Few-NERD 方向相同），\n      因为极端组构造直接操作 batch 内相似度，绕过了 centrality confound。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"MAVEN Count Curve (v2 prompt, 500 samples)\"\n        columns: [\"count\", \"relaxed_F1\", \"exact_F1\", \"recall\", \"precision\", \"pred_gold_ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.118, 0.011, 0.210, 0.082, 2.56]\n          - [6, 0.142, 0.005, 0.185, 0.115, 1.61]\n          - [12, 0.178, 0.010, 0.210, 0.154, 1.36]\n          - [22, 0.210, 0.015, 0.238, 0.188, 1.27]\n          - [44, 0.248, 0.020, 0.268, 0.231, 1.16]\n          - [64, 0.261, 0.016, 0.275, 0.249, 1.10]\n      - title: \"MAVEN Pairwise SCS → Confusion (2×2 embedding comparison)\"\n        columns: [\"embedding\", \"pearson_r\", \"p-value\", \"n_pairs\", \"verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"MiniLM\", 0.120, \"1.2e-45\", 14028, \"PASS\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3\", -0.007, 0.41, 14028, \"FAIL\"]\n      - title: \"MAVEN Per-type BCS → F1 (centrality confound)\"\n        columns: [\"embedding\", \"spearman_ρ\", \"p-value\", \"direction\", \"verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"MiniLM\", 0.208, 0.011, \"positive\", \"CONFOUND\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3\", 0.189, 0.021, \"positive\", \"CONFOUND\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN count curve (relaxed F1) — F1 单调递增（与 Few-NERD 相反），显示同质 schema 的 count-context 效应\"\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN pairwise SCS vs confusion rate scatter (MiniLM) — r=0.120，高 SCS 对有更多 confusion\"\n      - \"Fig: centrality confound 示意图 — mean BCS vs type frequency (r=0.34) + mean BCS vs F1 (ρ=+0.21) 的双重正相关链\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 结果完美支持论文的两层叙事：（1）pairwise confusability 在第三个任务（ED）上独立复现，\n      跨 NER→RE→ED 三任务验证 Claim 1；（2）per-type centrality confound 是方法论贡献——\n      解释了为什么简单的 per-type 聚合（如直接用 mean BCS 排序类型）在同质 schema 上失效，\n      而 pairwise 分析和 SDGD 的 pairwise 操作策略绕过了这个问题。\n      Exact F1 极低（<0.02）是 event trigger 边界匹配问题，不影响 confusability 分析（使用 relaxed F1）。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-005: DocRED 扩展验证\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"DocRED Confusability Study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      在 DocRED 96 关系类型上进行 count curve + pairwise SCS→confusion 分析。\n      文档级 RE 任务，更长的上下文，测试 confusability 信号在复杂推理场景下的鲁棒性。\n    expected_results:\n      count_curve_f1:\n        count_1: 0.195\n        count_6: 0.168\n        count_12: 0.152\n        count_24: 0.131\n        count_48: 0.118\n        count_96: 0.098\n      pairwise_miniLM:\n        n_pairs: 4560\n        pearson_r: 0.108\n        pearson_p: 3.5e-13\n        spearman_rho: 0.122\n        spearman_p: 1.8e-16\n      per_type_qwen3:\n        n_types: 82\n        filter: \"freq>=5\"\n        spearman_rho: -0.231\n        spearman_p: 0.037\n      extreme_batch_comparison:\n        count_12_high_bcs_f1: 0.105\n        count_12_low_bcs_f1: 0.188\n        delta_pp: -8.3\n        confusion_rate_ratio: 5.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      DocRED 关系类型语义分布介于 Few-NERD（跨域）和 MAVEN（同域）之间——\n      96 个关系覆盖多个领域但部分关系高度相似（如 \"place of birth\" vs \"place of death\"）。\n      Pairwise 信号成立但效应略弱于 Few-NERD（r=0.108 vs 0.156），因为文档级 RE 中\n      更长的上下文提供了更多消歧信息，部分缓解了 confusability 效应。\n      Per-type 方向正确（负相关），因为 DocRED 跨域程度足够避免 MAVEN 的 centrality confound。\n      Extreme batch delta 较小（8.3pp vs Few-NERD 的 20-50pp），同样因为文档级上下文的缓冲效应。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"DocRED Pairwise Comparison Across Embeddings\"\n        columns: [\"embedding\", \"pearson_r\", \"p-value\", \"verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"MiniLM\", 0.108, \"3.5e-13\", \"PASS\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3\", 0.095, \"2.1e-10\", \"PASS\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: DocRED count curve — F1 单调递减，与 Few-NERD 方向一致\"\n      - \"Fig: DocRED pairwise scatter — r=0.108，信号弱于 Few-NERD 但高度显著\"\n    analysis: >\n      DocRED 作为第四个任务验证了 pairwise confusability 信号的跨任务泛化性。\n      效应量较小但 n_pairs 足够保证统计显著。文档级上下文的缓冲效应是合理的——\n      更长的文档为模型提供了更多消歧证据。这一结果支持在论文中加入 DocRED 作为\n      supplementary evidence，但不改变三任务核心叙事。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-006: Interaction 2×2 析因\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Count × Confusability Interaction (2×2)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      在 Few-NERD 上构造 {低 count=6, 高 count=22} × {低 BCS, 高 BCS} 四组，\n      每组 10 batches，测试 count 和 confusability 的加法/乘法交互效应。\n    expected_results:\n      factorial_f1:\n        low_count_low_bcs: 0.372\n        low_count_high_bcs: 0.268\n        high_count_low_bcs: 0.312\n        high_count_high_bcs: 0.178\n      factorial_recall:\n        low_count_low_bcs: 0.468\n        low_count_high_bcs: 0.415\n        high_count_low_bcs: 0.330\n        high_count_high_bcs: 0.265\n      factorial_type_confusion_rate:\n        low_count_low_bcs: 0.008\n        low_count_high_bcs: 0.045\n        high_count_low_bcs: 0.018\n        high_count_high_bcs: 0.072\n      two_way_anova:\n        count_main_effect_F: 14.2\n        count_main_effect_p: 0.0006\n        bcs_main_effect_F: 22.8\n        bcs_main_effect_p: 3.1e-5\n        interaction_F: 3.1\n        interaction_p: 0.087\n        interaction_verdict: \"边际显著，轻微超加性\"\n      effect_decomposition:\n        count_delta_f1: -0.075\n        bcs_delta_f1: -0.119\n        interaction_delta_f1: -0.027\n        additive_prediction_high_high: 0.197\n        actual_high_high: 0.178\n        super_additive_gap: -0.019\n    result_rationale: >\n      Count 和 confusability 通过不同机制降低性能：count 稀释 attention → recall 下降，\n      confusability 引起类型混淆 → precision 下降。两者理论上正交，但在 high-count high-BCS 条件下\n      存在轻微超加性——当 attention 已被稀释时，模型对类型区分的余量更小，confusability 的边际伤害更大。\n      交互效应统计上边际显著（p=0.087），不足以拒绝加法模型，这恰好支持论文的\"正交通道\"叙事：\n      两个通道基本独立，各自可寻址。超加性的微弱存在（1.9pp gap）在讨论中作为 nuance 提及。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"2×2 Factorial F1 Results\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Low BCS\", \"High BCS\", \"BCS effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Low count (6)\", 0.372, 0.268, \"-0.104\"]\n          - [\"High count (22)\", 0.312, 0.178, \"-0.134\"]\n          - [\"Count effect\", \"-0.060\", \"-0.090\", \"interaction: -0.027\"]\n      - title: \"2×2 Type Confusion Rate\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Low BCS\", \"High BCS\", \"ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Low count (6)\", 0.008, 0.045, \"5.6x\"]\n          - [\"High count (22)\", 0.018, 0.072, \"4.0x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 2×2 interaction plot (F1) — 两条近似平行线，高 count 线略陡，显示微弱超加性\"\n      - \"Fig: 2×2 interaction plot (type confusion rate) — 交叉放大，high-count high-BCS 显著最高\"\n    analysis: >\n      2×2 结果核心支持 multi-channel 正交模型。BCS 主效应（F=22.8）大于 count 主效应（F=14.2），\n      说明在 Few-NERD 上 confusability 是更强的降级因子。交互效应 p=0.087 表明实质上加法模型足够，\n      轻微超加性可在论文中讨论但不改变核心叙事。这一结果直接支持 SDGD 的设计原理：\n      单独优化 batch 内 confusability（而非同时优化 count）已经足够捕获大部分可分解的性能损失。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-007: Error Taxonomy\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Systematic Error Taxonomy\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      在 exp-002 数据上系统分类 FP 错误为四类：type_substitution、boundary_error、\n      false_negative、hallucination，按 BCS quartile 分 bin 统计分布。\n    expected_results:\n      error_distribution_by_bcs_quartile:\n        Q1_low_bcs:\n          type_substitution_pct: 6.2\n          boundary_error_pct: 14.8\n          false_negative_pct: 58.3\n          hallucination_pct: 20.7\n          total_errors: 385\n        Q2:\n          type_substitution_pct: 12.5\n          boundary_error_pct: 13.2\n          false_negative_pct: 51.8\n          hallucination_pct: 22.5\n          total_errors: 412\n        Q3:\n          type_substitution_pct: 22.1\n          boundary_error_pct: 11.9\n          false_negative_pct: 44.6\n          hallucination_pct: 21.4\n          total_errors: 448\n        Q4_high_bcs:\n          type_substitution_pct: 38.4\n          boundary_error_pct: 10.5\n          false_negative_pct: 32.3\n          hallucination_pct: 18.8\n          total_errors: 521\n      monotonic_trends:\n        type_substitution_vs_bcs: \"单调递增 6.2→38.4%，Kendall τ=0.92\"\n        false_negative_vs_bcs: \"单调递减 58.3→32.3%，Kendall τ=-0.88\"\n        boundary_error_vs_bcs: \"微弱递减 14.8→10.5%，不显著\"\n        hallucination_vs_bcs: \"无趋势 20.7→18.8%，Kendall τ=-0.21\"\n      by_count_level:\n        count_6:\n          Q1_type_sub_pct: 4.8\n          Q4_type_sub_pct: 31.2\n          Q1_fn_pct: 61.5\n          Q4_fn_pct: 38.1\n        count_12:\n          Q1_type_sub_pct: 7.9\n          Q4_type_sub_pct: 44.7\n          Q1_fn_pct: 54.2\n          Q4_fn_pct: 27.8\n      chi_squared_bcs_vs_error_type:\n        statistic: 89.4\n        p: 1.2e-16\n        df: 9\n    result_rationale: >\n      Type substitution 与 BCS 强单调递增是 Claim 2 的核心机械证据：高 confusability batch 中，\n      模型正确识别了 entity span 但将其标注为语义邻近的错误类型。这是 confusability 通道的签名错误。\n      False negative 与 BCS 递减是因为在高 BCS batch 中，模型更倾向于\"猜错类型\"而非\"完全遗漏\"——\n      当多个相似类型在 prompt 中共现时，模型被激活去标注更多 span，但标注质量下降。\n      Hallucination 和 boundary error 与 BCS 无关，因为它们由其他因素驱动（幻觉=模型先验偏差，\n      边界=tokenization/span 识别问题），与类型相似度正交。\n      这一分解证实了 multi-channel 模型：count→omission(FN)，confusability→substitution。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Error Type Distribution by BCS Quartile (%)\"\n        columns: [\"BCS quartile\", \"Type sub.\", \"Boundary\", \"False neg.\", \"Halluc.\", \"Total\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Q1 (low)\", 6.2, 14.8, 58.3, 20.7, 385]\n          - [\"Q2\", 12.5, 13.2, 51.8, 22.5, 412]\n          - [\"Q3\", 22.1, 11.9, 44.6, 21.4, 448]\n          - [\"Q4 (high)\", 38.4, 10.5, 32.3, 18.8, 521]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: stacked bar chart — 四类错误按 BCS quartile 的占比变化，type_sub 从底部明显膨胀\"\n      - \"Fig: dual-axis plot — type_substitution rate (左轴, 递增) vs false_negative rate (右轴, 递减) 随 BCS quartile\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error taxonomy 是 Claim 2（multi-channel degradation）最直接的机械证据。\n      Type substitution 从 Q1 的 6.2% 飙升到 Q4 的 38.4%（6.2x），而 false negative 反向变化，\n      hallucination 稳定。这精确对应 multi-channel 模型的预测：confusability 通道选择性地增加\n      类型混淆错误，而非所有类型错误。count_12 条件下效应更强（Q4 type_sub=44.7%），\n      因为更多类型在 prompt 中同时出现时，confusability 的累积效应更大。\n      Chi-squared 高度显著（p=1.2e-16）确认 BCS quartile 与错误类型分布非独立。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-008: SDGD-zero on Few-NERD (R2)\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero Few-NERD (R2 revision)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-zero R2：修复 R1 的阈值和合并策略问题。基于 Qwen3 embedding pairwise SCS，\n      构建 confusability graph（阈值 τ=0.82），图着色分组，每组独立推理后合并。\n      对比 single-pass full-schema baseline。\n    expected_results:\n      r2_fixes:\n        threshold: \"τ=0.82 (R1 used 0.90, too aggressive → batches still confusable)\"\n        merge_strategy: \"span-level confidence dedup with type priority (R1 used naive union → duplicate spans)\"\n        batch_config: \"8 batches, avg 8.25 types/batch (range: 6-11)\"\n      sdgd_zero_results:\n        f1: 0.469\n        precision: 0.548\n        recall: 0.410\n        n_api_calls: 8\n        wall_clock_minutes: 12.5\n      single_pass_baseline:\n        f1: 0.414\n        precision: 0.648\n        recall: 0.304\n        n_api_calls: 1\n        wall_clock_minutes: 2.8\n      delta_vs_singlepass:\n        delta_f1_pp: 5.5\n        delta_recall_pp: 10.6\n        delta_precision_pp: -10.0\n        f1_p_value: 0.003\n        verdict: \"PASS — F1 显著提升，recall 大幅改善，precision 可控下降\"\n      per_batch_analysis:\n        mean_batch_bcs: 0.762\n        max_batch_bcs: 0.801\n        min_batch_bcs: 0.718\n        singlepass_bcs: 0.847\n        bcs_reduction_pct: 10.0\n      batch_level_breakdown:\n        batch_1: {n_types: 8, bcs: 0.738, f1: 0.385}\n        batch_2: {n_types: 9, bcs: 0.762, f1: 0.352}\n        batch_3: {n_types: 7, bcs: 0.721, f1: 0.401}\n        batch_4: {n_types: 11, bcs: 0.801, f1: 0.312}\n        batch_5: {n_types: 8, bcs: 0.745, f1: 0.378}\n        batch_6: {n_types: 9, bcs: 0.773, f1: 0.345}\n        batch_7: {n_types: 8, bcs: 0.752, f1: 0.368}\n        batch_8: {n_types: 6, bcs: 0.718, f1: 0.415}\n      type_confusion_rate:\n        sdgd_zero: 0.021\n        single_pass: 0.038\n        reduction_pct: 44.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      R1 失败的根因是两个实现问题：（1）SCS 阈值 τ=0.90 过高，导致 confusability graph 过于稀疏，\n      图着色产生的分组仍包含大量高相似度对（0.82-0.90 范围被遗漏）；\n      （2）naive union merge 在多个 batch 对同一 span 产生不同类型标注时直接取并集，\n      引入大量重复和矛盾预测。R2 将 τ 降至 0.82（基于 Few-NERD pairwise SCS 分布的 P90），\n      确保 top-10% 相似度对被强制分离；merge 策略改为 span-level confidence dedup，\n      当多个 batch 对同一 text span 产生不同类型时取置信度最高者。\n      F1 从 0.414 提升至 0.469（+5.5pp）主要来自 recall 改善（+10.6pp）：\n      较小的 batch（8 types vs 66 types）显著减少了 attention dilution，模型遗漏更少的 entity。\n      Precision 下降（-10.0pp）因为 8 个 batch 的合并引入了少量 spurious predictions，\n      但 confidence-based merge 将其控制在可接受范围。\n      净 F1 收益 +5.5pp 在 [3, 8] 范围中部，合理反映了 zero-shot 图着色方法的局限——\n      embedding 相似度只是 empirical confusability 的代理，最优分组需要 calibration data（→ exp-010）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"SDGD-zero R2 vs Single-pass on Few-NERD (66 types)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Precision\", \"Recall\", \"API calls\", \"Wall-clock (min)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass\", 0.414, 0.648, 0.304, 1, 2.8]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero R2\", 0.469, 0.548, 0.410, 8, 12.5]\n          - [\"Δ\", \"+5.5pp\", \"-10.0pp\", \"+10.6pp\", \"+7\", \"+9.7\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: F1/Precision/Recall bar chart — SDGD-zero vs single-pass，显示 F1 净提升来自 recall 的大幅改善\"\n      - \"Fig: per-batch BCS vs F1 scatter — 8 个 batch 内部，低 BCS batch 有更高 F1，验证 confusability-aware 分组的有效性\"\n      - \"Fig: merge 前后 prediction overlap 热力图 — 展示 confidence dedup 的效果\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-zero R2 的成功直接验证了 Claim 3：confusability-aware 分组本身有价值。\n      +5.5 F1 pp 中，约 2.2pp 来自 count reduction（见 exp-013），3.3pp 来自 confusability-aware grouping。\n      Per-batch 分析显示 batch 4（BCS=0.801, F1=0.312）vs batch 8（BCS=0.718, F1=0.415）\n      的对比直接体现了 SDGD 的内部一致性——即使在 SDGD 的优化分组内，\n      残余 confusability 差异仍然预测性能差异。\n      Type confusion rate 下降 44.7% 是机械证据：SDGD 通过分离 confusable pair 直接减少了 Channel 2 错误。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-009: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-zero 在 MAVEN 168 event types 上的 cross-task 验证。\n      基于 MiniLM embedding（MAVEN 上有效的 pairwise proxy），graph coloring 分组。\n    expected_results:\n      sdgd_zero_results:\n        relaxed_f1: 0.305\n        exact_f1: 0.022\n        n_batches: 14\n        avg_types_per_batch: 12.0\n        n_api_calls: 14\n        wall_clock_minutes: 22.4\n      single_pass_baseline:\n        relaxed_f1: 0.272\n        exact_f1: 0.014\n        n_api_calls: 1\n        wall_clock_minutes: 4.2\n      random_batching_baseline:\n        relaxed_f1: 0.282\n        n_api_calls: 14\n      delta_vs_singlepass:\n        delta_relaxed_f1_pp: 3.3\n        p_value: 0.012\n      delta_vs_random:\n        delta_relaxed_f1_pp: 2.3\n        p_value: 0.038\n      type_confusion_reduction:\n        sdgd_zero_rate: 0.035\n        single_pass_rate: 0.058\n        reduction_pct: 39.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 上 SDGD 收益（+3.3pp relaxed F1）小于 Few-NERD（+5.5pp），原因有二：\n      （1）MAVEN 的 SCS 分布更集中（mean=0.216, std=0.103），图着色的\"分离空间\"更小，\n      无法像 Few-NERD 那样找到明确的低相似度分组；\n      （2）MAVEN F1 与 count 正相关（exp-004），batch 缩小到 12 types 会损失部分 count-context 效益，\n      部分抵消了 confusability reduction 的收益。\n      使用 MiniLM 而非 Qwen3 是正确选择，因为 MiniLM pairwise 信号在 MAVEN 上有效（r=0.120）而 Qwen3 无效。\n      vs random 的 +2.3pp 确认 confusability-aware 分组在同质 schema 上仍然有价值，\n      尽管收益小于跨域 schema。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"SDGD-zero on MAVEN (168 types, MiniLM embedding)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Relaxed F1\", \"Exact F1\", \"API calls\", \"Δ relaxed F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass (168 types)\", 0.272, 0.014, 1, \"—\"]\n          - [\"Random batching (k=14)\", 0.282, 0.017, 14, \"+1.0pp\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero (k=14)\", 0.305, 0.022, 14, \"+3.3pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN 三方法对比 bar chart — 显示 SDGD > random > single-pass\"\n      - \"Fig: SDGD vs random per-batch scatter — SDGD batch 的 BCS 更低且方差更小\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 上的正向结果完成 SDGD 的 cross-task 验证（NER + ED），\n      证明 confusability-aware 分组在不同任务和 schema 特征下均有效。\n      效应量较小但仍然显著（p=0.012 vs single-pass），足以支持 Claim 3。\n      值得注意的是 embedding 选择的重要性——在 MAVEN 上使用 Qwen3 embedding 的 SDGD\n      可能无效（因为 Qwen3 pairwise 信号不显著），这强化了论文中\"task-appropriate embedding\"的建议。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-010: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal Few-NERD\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-cal：使用 5-10 calibration examples 构建经验 confusion matrix，\n      替代 embedding SCS 作为 confusability proxy，再用 graph coloring 分组。\n      对比 SDGD-zero。\n    expected_results:\n      calibration_cost:\n        n_calibration_examples: 8\n        n_calibration_api_calls: 8\n        calibration_wall_clock_minutes: 4.5\n      sdgd_cal_results:\n        f1: 0.488\n        precision: 0.556\n        recall: 0.435\n        n_api_calls: 9\n        wall_clock_minutes: 14.2\n        total_api_calls_incl_calibration: 17\n      sdgd_zero_comparison:\n        sdgd_zero_f1: 0.469\n        delta_f1_pp: 1.9\n        p_value: 0.042\n      calibration_vs_embedding_correlation:\n        empirical_vs_qwen3_scs_spearman: 0.58\n        empirical_vs_miniLM_scs_spearman: 0.43\n        verdict: \"经验 confusability 与 embedding proxy 中等相关，但经验版更准确\"\n      confusion_matrix_properties:\n        n_nonzero_pairs: 312\n        n_total_pairs: 2145\n        sparsity: 0.854\n        top_empirical_pair: \"person-other ↔ person-politician (confusion=23/8 examples)\"\n        top_embedding_pair: \"same pair (BCS=0.934)\"\n        agreement_top_20: \"85% overlap\"\n        disagreement_examples: \"building-library ↔ building-theater (high SCS=0.91, low empirical=0)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 高 1.9 F1 pp，因为经验 confusion matrix 直接捕获了\n      LLM 的实际混淆模式，而 embedding SCS 只是语义相似度的代理。\n      两者差距不大（1.9pp）因为 embedding proxy 已经相当好——top-20 confusable pairs 有 85% 重叠。\n      差异主要来自 edge cases：某些 embedding 上高相似但 LLM 实际不混淆的 pair\n      （如 building-library ↔ building-theater，LLM 依靠上下文线索有效区分），\n      以及 embedding 上不相似但 LLM 实际混淆的 pair（可能由于 training data 偏差）。\n      Calibration 的额外成本（8 API calls）使总 API calls 从 8 增至 17，\n      但仍远低于 per-type splitting（66 calls），且 F1 接近 per-type 水平。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"SDGD Variant Comparison on Few-NERD\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"P\", \"R\", \"API calls (total)\", \"Δ F1 vs single-pass\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass\", 0.414, 0.648, 0.304, 1, \"—\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero\", 0.469, 0.548, 0.410, 8, \"+5.5pp\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-cal\", 0.488, 0.556, 0.435, 17, \"+7.4pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: empirical confusion matrix heatmap (top-30 types) — 可视化实际混淆模式\"\n      - \"Fig: SCS vs empirical confusion scatter — r=0.58，验证 embedding proxy 的合理性和局限性\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-cal 的 +1.9pp 增量验证了 SDGD 框架的可扩展性——更好的 confusability 估计\n      直接转化为更好的分组和更高的 F1。这也为 SDGD-zero 的实用性提供了参照：\n      在无 calibration data 的冷启动场景下，SDGD-zero 已能获得大部分收益（5.5/7.4 = 74%），\n      calibration 的边际收益递减。论文中 SDGD-zero 作为默认推荐，SDGD-cal 作为高精度选项。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-011: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-cal 在 MAVEN 168 types 上的完整对比。\n      使用 MiniLM embedding 和 10 calibration examples。\n    expected_results:\n      sdgd_cal_results:\n        relaxed_f1: 0.318\n        exact_f1: 0.025\n        n_api_calls: 14\n        total_api_calls_incl_calibration: 24\n      full_comparison_table:\n        single_pass: {relaxed_f1: 0.272, api_calls: 1}\n        random_k14: {relaxed_f1: 0.282, api_calls: 14}\n        sdgd_zero_miniLM: {relaxed_f1: 0.305, api_calls: 14}\n        sdgd_cal: {relaxed_f1: 0.318, api_calls: 24}\n        per_type: {relaxed_f1: 0.325, api_calls: 168}\n      delta_sdgd_cal_vs_zero: \"+1.3pp\"\n      delta_sdgd_cal_vs_singlepass: \"+4.6pp\"\n      calibration_improvement_on_maven:\n        empirical_vs_miniLM_spearman: 0.49\n        verdict: \"经验混淆信号在同质 schema 上增量更大，因为 embedding 信号更弱（MiniLM r=0.120）\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 上 SDGD-cal vs SDGD-zero 的增量（1.3pp）与 Few-NERD 的（1.9pp）相近，\n      因为 calibration data 在同质 schema 上的价值更高——MiniLM embedding 在 MAVEN 上\n      虽然 pairwise 信号显著但效应较弱（r=0.120 vs Few-NERD Qwen3 r=0.156），\n      经验数据能更精确地识别实际高混淆对。\n      SDGD-cal（0.318）接近 per-type splitting（0.325）但 API calls 少 7x（24 vs 168），\n      完成 SDGD 框架在效率/质量 tradeoff 上的定位。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Full Comparison Table: MAVEN (168 types)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Relaxed F1\", \"API calls\", \"Δ vs single-pass\", \"Latency ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass\", 0.272, 1, \"—\", \"1.0x\"]\n          - [\"Random (k=14)\", 0.282, 14, \"+1.0pp\", \"5.3x\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero (MiniLM)\", 0.305, 14, \"+3.3pp\", \"5.3x\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-cal\", 0.318, 24, \"+4.6pp\", \"8.5x\"]\n          - [\"Per-type (k=168)\", 0.325, 168, \"+5.3pp\", \"40.0x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN full method comparison — F1 vs API calls Pareto plot，SDGD-cal 位于 Pareto 前沿\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 完整对比表是论文 Table 3（或 4）的核心内容。SDGD-cal 在 Pareto 前沿上\n      明确优于 random 和 single-pass，接近 per-type 但成本大幅降低。\n      这完成了 Claim 3 的全部证据链：confusability-aware 分组在两个任务上均有效，\n      且 SDGD 框架提供了从 zero-shot 到 calibrated 的灵活选项。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-012: Multi-model (LLaMA-3.3-70B)\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Multi-model Validation (LLaMA-3.3-70B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: >\n      用 LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct 在 Few-NERD 上复现 exp-002 协议：\n      count curve + extreme/random batch + pairwise/per-type 分析。\n    expected_results:\n      count_curve:\n        count_1: {f1: 0.298, recall: 0.612, precision: 0.198}\n        count_6: {f1: 0.275, recall: 0.445, precision: 0.200}\n        count_12: {f1: 0.318, recall: 0.312, precision: 0.324}\n        count_22: {f1: 0.282, recall: 0.258, precision: 0.311}\n        count_44: {f1: 0.405, recall: 0.370, precision: 0.447}\n        count_64: {f1: 0.378, recall: 0.288, precision: 0.548}\n      pairwise_analysis:\n        qwen3_embedding:\n          n_pairs: 1953\n          pearson_r: 0.138\n          pearson_p: 3.2e-9\n          spearman_rho: 0.144\n          spearman_p: 8.1e-10\n          nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.228\n          nonzero_spearman_p: 5.7e-5\n        miniLM_embedding:\n          pearson_r: 0.072\n          pearson_p: 0.0015\n      per_type_analysis:\n        n_types: 60\n        filter: \"freq>=5\"\n        qwen3_spearman_rho: -0.265\n        qwen3_spearman_p: 0.041\n        miniLM_spearman_rho: -0.058\n        miniLM_spearman_p: 0.66\n      extreme_batch:\n        count_6_high_bcs_f1: 0.195\n        count_6_low_bcs_f1: 0.342\n        count_12_high_bcs_f1: 0.215\n        count_12_low_bcs_f1: 0.398\n        confusion_rate_ratio_count6: 18.5\n        confusion_rate_ratio_count12: 12.3\n      cross_model_comparison:\n        qwen3_pairwise_r: 0.156\n        llama_pairwise_r: 0.138\n        delta: -0.018\n        both_significant: true\n        fisher_z_test_p: 0.52\n        verdict: \"效应量无显著差异，two models 一致\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA-3.3-70B 的 pairwise r=0.138 略低于 Qwen3 的 0.156，因为不同模型的\n      confusability 敏感度略有差异——LLaMA 的指令遵从能力更强（70B 参数 + Instruct 调优），\n      可能在部分高 confusability pair 上仍能正确区分。但差异不显著（Fisher z p=0.52），\n      确认 confusability signal 是跨模型稳定的现象。\n      Per-type ρ=-0.265（p=0.041）方向和显著性与 Qwen3（ρ=-0.293, p=0.020）一致，\n      说明 Few-NERD 的跨域 schema 结构使 per-type 信号在不同提取模型上均稳定。\n      Extreme batch confusion rate ratio 12-18x 与 Qwen3 的 10-28x 范围一致。\n      LLaMA 整体 F1 略低于 Qwen3（count_64: 0.378 vs 0.414），可能因为 LLaMA 的\n      NER 提示模板适配度稍差，但不影响 confusability 信号的相对模式。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-model Pairwise Comparison on Few-NERD\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Embedding\", \"Pearson r\", \"p-value\", \"Spearman ρ\", \"p-value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"Qwen3\", 0.156, \"4.6e-12\", 0.160, \"1.3e-12\"]\n          - [\"LLaMA-3.3-70B\", \"Qwen3\", 0.138, \"3.2e-9\", 0.144, \"8.1e-10\"]\n          - [\"Fisher z-test\", \"—\", \"Δ=0.018\", \"p=0.52\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n      - title: \"Cross-model Extreme Batch Confusion Rate\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Count\", \"High-BCS rate\", \"Low-BCS rate\", \"Ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", 6, 0.0728, 0.0014, \"27.5x\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", 12, 0.0480, 0.0061, \"9.9x\"]\n          - [\"LLaMA-70B\", 6, 0.0612, 0.0033, \"18.5x\"]\n          - [\"LLaMA-70B\", 12, 0.0445, 0.0036, \"12.3x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 双模型 pairwise scatter overlay — Qwen3 (蓝) vs LLaMA (橙)，回归线斜率接近\"\n      - \"Fig: cross-model confusion rate ratio comparison — 两模型一致的 high/low BCS 差异模式\"\n    analysis: >\n      Multi-model 验证完成 cross_model_significant: 2/2 的要求。两个差异显著的架构\n      （Qwen3-32B decoder vs LLaMA-3.3-70B decoder）在 pairwise confusability signal、\n      per-type direction、extreme batch effect 上全部一致，排除了单模型 artifact 的可能性。\n      Fisher z-test 的 p=0.52 确认两模型效应量无统计差异。\n      这是对 reviewer concern \"only one model\" 的完整回应。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-013: Random Batching Ablation\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Random Batching Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      与 SDGD-zero 相同的 k=8 batch count，但 batch composition 完全随机。\n      5 次随机种子取平均。隔离 confusability-aware grouping 的贡献。\n    expected_results:\n      random_batching_results:\n        mean_f1: 0.436\n        std_f1: 0.012\n        mean_precision: 0.530\n        mean_recall: 0.370\n        n_api_calls: 8\n        n_random_seeds: 5\n      comparison:\n        single_pass_f1: 0.414\n        sdgd_zero_f1: 0.469\n        random_f1: 0.436\n        delta_random_vs_singlepass: \"+2.2pp\"\n        delta_sdgd_vs_random: \"+3.3pp\"\n        delta_sdgd_vs_singlepass: \"+5.5pp\"\n      decomposition:\n        count_reduction_contribution: \"2.2pp (40% of total SDGD gain)\"\n        confusability_aware_contribution: \"3.3pp (60% of total SDGD gain)\"\n      random_batch_bcs_stats:\n        mean_batch_bcs: 0.838\n        std_batch_bcs: 0.025\n        sdgd_mean_batch_bcs: 0.762\n        bcs_reduction_by_sdgd: \"9.1%\"\n      type_confusion_rates:\n        random: 0.031\n        sdgd_zero: 0.021\n        single_pass: 0.038\n    result_rationale: >\n      Random batching 获得 +2.2pp 改善（vs single-pass）完全来自 count reduction：\n      从 66 types/batch 降到 ~8 types/batch 减少了 attention dilution，提升了 recall。\n      但 random batch 的 mean BCS（0.838）接近 single-pass（0.847），\n      因为随机分组不会系统性地分离 confusable pair。\n      SDGD-zero 的额外 +3.3pp 来自 confusability-aware grouping：mean batch BCS 降至 0.762，\n      type confusion rate 从 0.031 降至 0.021（32% 减少）。\n      60%/40% 的贡献分解表明 confusability-aware grouping 是 SDGD 价值的主要来源，\n      而非简单的 batch count reduction。这是 Claim 3 最关键的证据——\n      SDGD 优于 random batching（same k）直接证明了 confusability-aware 分组的独立价值。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Ablation: SDGD-zero vs Random Batching vs Single-pass\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Recall\", \"Type confusion rate\", \"Mean batch BCS\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass (k=1)\", 0.414, 0.304, 0.038, 0.847]\n          - [\"Random (k=8)\", 0.436, 0.370, 0.031, 0.838]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero (k=8)\", 0.469, 0.410, 0.021, 0.762]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: F1 gain decomposition waterfall chart — single-pass → +2.2pp (count) → +3.3pp (confusability) → SDGD\"\n      - \"Fig: 5 random seeds 的 F1 分布 + SDGD-zero 的位置（显著高于随机分布上界）\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是论文中最重要的 ablation。SDGD vs random（same k）的 +3.3pp gap（p < 0.01）\n      是 Claim 3 的充分必要证据——confusability-aware 分组本身有价值，\n      SDGD 的收益不仅仅来自简单的 schema 分解。\n      5 次随机种子的 std=0.012 表明 random batching 的方差较小，SDGD-zero 的 0.469\n      显著高于随机分布的上界（0.436 + 2×0.012 = 0.460），排除了 lucky draw 的可能性。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-014: Per-type Splitting (UniNER-style)\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Per-type Splitting Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      每个类型单独一个 batch（k=66），每次只提取一种类型。\n      UniNER-style 的上界实验。对比 SDGD 和 single-pass。\n    expected_results:\n      per_type_results:\n        f1: 0.475\n        precision: 0.512\n        recall: 0.443\n        n_api_calls: 66\n        wall_clock_minutes: 68.5\n      comparison:\n        single_pass: {f1: 0.414, api_calls: 1, wall_clock: 2.8}\n        random_k8: {f1: 0.436, api_calls: 8, wall_clock: 12.5}\n        sdgd_zero: {f1: 0.469, api_calls: 8, wall_clock: 12.5}\n        sdgd_cal: {f1: 0.488, api_calls: 17, wall_clock: 14.2}\n        per_type: {f1: 0.475, api_calls: 66, wall_clock: 68.5}\n      sdgd_zero_vs_per_type:\n        f1_gap: \"-0.6pp\"\n        api_calls_ratio: \"8.25x fewer\"\n        wall_clock_ratio: \"5.5x faster\"\n        verdict: \"SDGD-zero 达到 per-type 的 98.7% F1，但成本仅 12%\"\n      sdgd_cal_vs_per_type:\n        f1_gap: \"+1.3pp (SDGD-cal 更高)\"\n        api_calls_ratio: \"3.9x fewer\"\n        verdict: \"SDGD-cal 超过 per-type，因为保留了部分 cross-type 上下文\"\n      per_type_error_analysis:\n        type_confusion_rate: 0.002\n        false_negative_rate: 0.31\n        hallucination_rate: 0.28\n        boundary_error_rate: 0.16\n        note: \"type confusion 几乎消除，但 hallucination 上升——单类型 prompt 缺乏跨类型约束\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-type splitting 几乎消除了 type confusion（rate=0.002 vs single-pass 0.038），\n      验证了 confusability 是可通过分组解决的。但 F1 只有 0.475，低于预期的\"上界\"，\n      因为存在两个反向效应：\n      （1）缺乏 cross-type context：当只有一个类型时，模型无法利用\"这个 span 更像 X 而非 Y\"的对比信息，\n      导致某些模糊 span 被遗漏或被 hallucinate（hallucination rate 上升至 0.28）；\n      （2）recall 上升到 0.443（最高），因为 attention 完全集中在单一类型上。\n      SDGD-zero（0.469）接近 per-type（0.475）的原因是：SDGD 的 8-type batch 保留了\n      有限但有用的 cross-type context，同时移除了大部分 confusability。\n      SDGD-cal（0.488）超过 per-type（0.475）是关键发现——证明 optimal decomposition\n      不是\"最大分解\"而是\"最优 confusability/context tradeoff\"，SDGD 框架正好在此定位。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Full Method Comparison on Few-NERD (66 types)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"P\", \"R\", \"API calls\", \"Wall-clock\", \"Efficiency\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass\", 0.414, 0.648, 0.304, 1, \"2.8 min\", \"baseline\"]\n          - [\"Random (k=8)\", 0.436, 0.530, 0.370, 8, \"12.5 min\", \"+2.2pp / 8 calls\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero (k=8)\", 0.469, 0.548, 0.410, 8, \"12.5 min\", \"+5.5pp / 8 calls\"]\n          - [\"Per-type (k=66)\", 0.475, 0.512, 0.443, 66, \"68.5 min\", \"+6.1pp / 66 calls\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-cal (k=9)\", 0.488, 0.556, 0.435, 17, \"14.2 min\", \"+7.4pp / 17 calls\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: F1 vs API calls Pareto plot — SDGD-zero 和 SDGD-cal 在 Pareto 前沿，per-type 被 dominated\"\n      - \"Fig: error type composition comparison — per-type 消除 type_sub 但增加 hallucination\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-type 实验揭示了一个反直觉的结果：最大分解≠最优分解。\n      SDGD-cal 超过 per-type 因为保留了 cross-type context 带来的消歧能力。\n      这使论文的 method 贡献更强——SDGD 不仅仅是\"把类型分开\"的简单策略，\n      而是在 confusability reduction 和 context preservation 之间的 principled tradeoff，\n      graph coloring 框架正好 operationalize 了这个 tradeoff。\n      Pareto plot 是论文的核心 figure 之一：清晰展示 SDGD variants 在效率/质量空间的优势。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-015: SCS Validation\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SCS Proxy Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-015\"\n    description: >\n      用 exp-010 的经验 confusion matrix 作为 ground truth，验证 embedding SCS\n      作为 confusability proxy 的排序准确性。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen3_scs_vs_empirical:\n        spearman_rho: 0.584\n        spearman_p: 2.3e-18\n        kendall_tau: 0.421\n        kendall_p: 8.1e-15\n        top_20_overlap: 0.85\n        top_50_overlap: 0.72\n      miniLM_scs_vs_empirical:\n        spearman_rho: 0.432\n        spearman_p: 1.7e-10\n        kendall_tau: 0.312\n        kendall_p: 3.4e-8\n        top_20_overlap: 0.65\n        top_50_overlap: 0.54\n      precision_at_k:\n        qwen3_p_at_10: 0.90\n        qwen3_p_at_20: 0.85\n        qwen3_p_at_50: 0.72\n        miniLM_p_at_10: 0.70\n        miniLM_p_at_20: 0.65\n        miniLM_p_at_50: 0.54\n      failure_modes:\n        false_positive_scs: \"embedding 高相似但不混淆：通常是共享 supertype 但 subtype 名称足够区分\"\n        false_negative_scs: \"embedding 低相似但实际混淆：通常因共现频率或 prompt 位置效应\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen3 SCS 与经验 confusability 的 Spearman ρ=0.584 表明 embedding 是合理但非完美的代理。\n      相关性显著但不为 1 的原因：\n      （1）embedding 相似度捕获语义距离，而实际 confusion 还受 prompt 位置、类型名称字面相似性、\n      训练数据频率等非语义因素影响；\n      （2）Qwen3 embedding 来自指令调优后的最后一层，保留了较多任务相关信息，因此优于 MiniLM。\n      Top-20 的 85% 重叠解释了为什么 SDGD-zero 已经很有效——最 confusable 的 pair 大多被正确识别。\n      SDGD-cal 的增量主要来自修正那 15% 的错误排序。\n      Precision@k 在 top-10 最高（0.90），说明 embedding proxy 在识别\"最危险\"pair 时最可靠。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"SCS Proxy Validation\"\n        columns: [\"Embedding\", \"Spearman ρ\", \"Kendall τ\", \"Top-20 overlap\", \"P@10\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3\", 0.584, 0.421, \"85%\", 0.90]\n          - [\"MiniLM\", 0.432, 0.312, \"65%\", 0.70]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: SCS vs empirical confusion scatter (Qwen3) with Precision@k curve inset\"\n      - \"Fig: failure mode examples — 标注 FP (高 SCS 低 confusion) 和 FN (低 SCS 高 confusion) 的具体 pair\"\n    analysis: >\n      SCS validation 完成了 SDGD 框架的理论闭环：embedding SCS 是合理的 confusability proxy\n      （ρ=0.58），但经验数据更好（SDGD-cal > SDGD-zero）。\n      论文的实用建议：cold-start 用 SDGD-zero（Qwen3 embedding），\n      有少量 calibration data 后切换到 SDGD-cal。Qwen3 明显优于 MiniLM 作为 proxy\n      在 Few-NERD 上，但 MAVEN 上反转（→ 使用 task-appropriate embedding）。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17638,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17638},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b7ad92b-97f6-47f3-a0ef-2ecf2be282d0","uuid":"6893f8ed-e783-477d-990a-09363c6ec4dd"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":443889,"duration_api_ms":445069,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 framing 完全成立。三条 claim 无需调整：pairwise confusability 跨 3 任务 2 模型独立预测退化，\n  multi-channel 模型有 error taxonomy 支撑，SDGD-zero R2 修复后在 Few-NERD 和 MAVEN 上均显著优于 single-pass 和 random batching。\n  论文标题保持 \"analysis + method\" 双贡献定位。\n  Headline: \"Pairwise confusability predicts degradation (r=0.12–0.16) and SDGD yields +5.5 F1 on complex schemas.\"\n  EMNLP Main 无需降级。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-004: MAVEN 全量 confusability 研究\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"MAVEN Confusability Study (full)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      在 MAVEN 168 event types 上运行 v2 prompt，500 sample，完成 count curve、\n      batch-level BCS 对照、pairwise SCS→confusion 相关、per-type 分析及 centrality confound 量化。\n    expected_results:\n      count_curve_relaxed_f1:\n        count_1: 0.118\n        count_6: 0.142\n        count_12: 0.178\n        count_22: 0.210\n        count_44: 0.248\n        count_64: 0.261\n        count_168: 0.272\n      count_curve_exact_f1:\n        count_1: 0.011\n        count_6: 0.005\n        count_12: 0.010\n        count_22: 0.015\n        count_44: 0.020\n        count_64: 0.016\n        count_168: 0.014\n      pairwise_miniLM:\n        n_pairs: 14028\n        pearson_r: 0.120\n        pearson_p: 1.2e-45\n        spearman_rho: 0.135\n        spearman_p: 3.8e-58\n        nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.191\n        nonzero_spearman_p: 4.7e-4\n      pairwise_qwen3:\n        pearson_r: -0.007\n        pearson_p: 0.41\n        verdict: \"NOT_SIGNIFICANT — Qwen3 embeddings 无法在同质 schema 上捕获 pairwise signal\"\n      per_type_miniLM:\n        n_types: 148\n        filter: \"freq>=10\"\n        spearman_rho: 0.208\n        spearman_p: 0.011\n        direction: positive\n        verdict: \"CENTRALITY CONFOUND — 方向与假设相反\"\n      per_type_qwen3:\n        spearman_rho: 0.189\n        spearman_p: 0.021\n        direction: positive\n        verdict: \"CENTRALITY CONFOUND — 两种 embedding 方向一致，排除 embedding 压缩假说\"\n      centrality_analysis:\n        mean_bcs_vs_type_frequency_r: 0.34\n        mean_bcs_vs_type_frequency_p: 2.1e-5\n        interpretation: \"高 mean BCS = 语义中心类型 = 高频/LLM 更熟悉 = 更高 F1\"\n      batch_level_extreme:\n        count_6_high_bcs_relaxed_f1: 0.218\n        count_6_low_bcs_relaxed_f1: 0.098\n        count_12_high_bcs_relaxed_f1: 0.192\n        count_12_low_bcs_relaxed_f1: 0.114\n        confusion_rate_ratio_extreme_count6: 8.2\n        confusion_rate_ratio_extreme_count12: 6.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 168 个 event types 来自同一语义域（FrameNet 层级结构），SCS 分布高度集中\n      （mean=0.216, std=0.103），不像 Few-NERD 有跨域分离。\n      Pairwise MiniLM 信号成立（r=0.120）因为 MiniLM 的通用语义空间在细粒度事件类型间保留了足够区分度，\n      而 Qwen3 指令调优后的表征空间过度压缩了语义邻近类型。\n      Per-type 正方向是 centrality confound 的典型表现：在同质 schema 中，\n      mean BCS 高的类型恰好是语义网络的中心节点（如 \"Attack\", \"Meeting\"），\n      这些类型在训练语料中高频出现，LLM 先验知识更强，F1 自然更高。\n      这不是假设失败，而是方法论贡献——揭示了 per-type 聚合何时失效。\n      Batch-level 极端组对照仍然显示 high-BCS 组更高（与 Few-NERD 方向相同），\n      因为极端组构造直接操作 batch 内相似度，绕过了 centrality confound。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"MAVEN Count Curve (v2 prompt, 500 samples)\"\n        columns: [\"count\", \"relaxed_F1\", \"exact_F1\", \"recall\", \"precision\", \"pred_gold_ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.118, 0.011, 0.210, 0.082, 2.56]\n          - [6, 0.142, 0.005, 0.185, 0.115, 1.61]\n          - [12, 0.178, 0.010, 0.210, 0.154, 1.36]\n          - [22, 0.210, 0.015, 0.238, 0.188, 1.27]\n          - [44, 0.248, 0.020, 0.268, 0.231, 1.16]\n          - [64, 0.261, 0.016, 0.275, 0.249, 1.10]\n      - title: \"MAVEN Pairwise SCS → Confusion (2×2 embedding comparison)\"\n        columns: [\"embedding\", \"pearson_r\", \"p-value\", \"n_pairs\", \"verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"MiniLM\", 0.120, \"1.2e-45\", 14028, \"PASS\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3\", -0.007, 0.41, 14028, \"FAIL\"]\n      - title: \"MAVEN Per-type BCS → F1 (centrality confound)\"\n        columns: [\"embedding\", \"spearman_ρ\", \"p-value\", \"direction\", \"verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"MiniLM\", 0.208, 0.011, \"positive\", \"CONFOUND\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3\", 0.189, 0.021, \"positive\", \"CONFOUND\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN count curve (relaxed F1) — F1 单调递增（与 Few-NERD 相反），显示同质 schema 的 count-context 效应\"\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN pairwise SCS vs confusion rate scatter (MiniLM) — r=0.120，高 SCS 对有更多 confusion\"\n      - \"Fig: centrality confound 示意图 — mean BCS vs type frequency (r=0.34) + mean BCS vs F1 (ρ=+0.21) 的双重正相关链\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 结果完美支持论文的两层叙事：（1）pairwise confusability 在第三个任务（ED）上独立复现，\n      跨 NER→RE→ED 三任务验证 Claim 1；（2）per-type centrality confound 是方法论贡献——\n      解释了为什么简单的 per-type 聚合（如直接用 mean BCS 排序类型）在同质 schema 上失效，\n      而 pairwise 分析和 SDGD 的 pairwise 操作策略绕过了这个问题。\n      Exact F1 极低（<0.02）是 event trigger 边界匹配问题，不影响 confusability 分析（使用 relaxed F1）。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-005: DocRED 扩展验证\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"DocRED Confusability Study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      在 DocRED 96 关系类型上进行 count curve + pairwise SCS→confusion 分析。\n      文档级 RE 任务，更长的上下文，测试 confusability 信号在复杂推理场景下的鲁棒性。\n    expected_results:\n      count_curve_f1:\n        count_1: 0.195\n        count_6: 0.168\n        count_12: 0.152\n        count_24: 0.131\n        count_48: 0.118\n        count_96: 0.098\n      pairwise_miniLM:\n        n_pairs: 4560\n        pearson_r: 0.108\n        pearson_p: 3.5e-13\n        spearman_rho: 0.122\n        spearman_p: 1.8e-16\n      per_type_qwen3:\n        n_types: 82\n        filter: \"freq>=5\"\n        spearman_rho: -0.231\n        spearman_p: 0.037\n      extreme_batch_comparison:\n        count_12_high_bcs_f1: 0.105\n        count_12_low_bcs_f1: 0.188\n        delta_pp: -8.3\n        confusion_rate_ratio: 5.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      DocRED 关系类型语义分布介于 Few-NERD（跨域）和 MAVEN（同域）之间——\n      96 个关系覆盖多个领域但部分关系高度相似（如 \"place of birth\" vs \"place of death\"）。\n      Pairwise 信号成立但效应略弱于 Few-NERD（r=0.108 vs 0.156），因为文档级 RE 中\n      更长的上下文提供了更多消歧信息，部分缓解了 confusability 效应。\n      Per-type 方向正确（负相关），因为 DocRED 跨域程度足够避免 MAVEN 的 centrality confound。\n      Extreme batch delta 较小（8.3pp vs Few-NERD 的 20-50pp），同样因为文档级上下文的缓冲效应。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"DocRED Pairwise Comparison Across Embeddings\"\n        columns: [\"embedding\", \"pearson_r\", \"p-value\", \"verdict\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"MiniLM\", 0.108, \"3.5e-13\", \"PASS\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3\", 0.095, \"2.1e-10\", \"PASS\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: DocRED count curve — F1 单调递减，与 Few-NERD 方向一致\"\n      - \"Fig: DocRED pairwise scatter — r=0.108，信号弱于 Few-NERD 但高度显著\"\n    analysis: >\n      DocRED 作为第四个任务验证了 pairwise confusability 信号的跨任务泛化性。\n      效应量较小但 n_pairs 足够保证统计显著。文档级上下文的缓冲效应是合理的——\n      更长的文档为模型提供了更多消歧证据。这一结果支持在论文中加入 DocRED 作为\n      supplementary evidence，但不改变三任务核心叙事。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-006: Interaction 2×2 析因\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Count × Confusability Interaction (2×2)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      在 Few-NERD 上构造 {低 count=6, 高 count=22} × {低 BCS, 高 BCS} 四组，\n      每组 10 batches，测试 count 和 confusability 的加法/乘法交互效应。\n    expected_results:\n      factorial_f1:\n        low_count_low_bcs: 0.372\n        low_count_high_bcs: 0.268\n        high_count_low_bcs: 0.312\n        high_count_high_bcs: 0.178\n      factorial_recall:\n        low_count_low_bcs: 0.468\n        low_count_high_bcs: 0.415\n        high_count_low_bcs: 0.330\n        high_count_high_bcs: 0.265\n      factorial_type_confusion_rate:\n        low_count_low_bcs: 0.008\n        low_count_high_bcs: 0.045\n        high_count_low_bcs: 0.018\n        high_count_high_bcs: 0.072\n      two_way_anova:\n        count_main_effect_F: 14.2\n        count_main_effect_p: 0.0006\n        bcs_main_effect_F: 22.8\n        bcs_main_effect_p: 3.1e-5\n        interaction_F: 3.1\n        interaction_p: 0.087\n        interaction_verdict: \"边际显著，轻微超加性\"\n      effect_decomposition:\n        count_delta_f1: -0.075\n        bcs_delta_f1: -0.119\n        interaction_delta_f1: -0.027\n        additive_prediction_high_high: 0.197\n        actual_high_high: 0.178\n        super_additive_gap: -0.019\n    result_rationale: >\n      Count 和 confusability 通过不同机制降低性能：count 稀释 attention → recall 下降，\n      confusability 引起类型混淆 → precision 下降。两者理论上正交，但在 high-count high-BCS 条件下\n      存在轻微超加性——当 attention 已被稀释时，模型对类型区分的余量更小，confusability 的边际伤害更大。\n      交互效应统计上边际显著（p=0.087），不足以拒绝加法模型，这恰好支持论文的\"正交通道\"叙事：\n      两个通道基本独立，各自可寻址。超加性的微弱存在（1.9pp gap）在讨论中作为 nuance 提及。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"2×2 Factorial F1 Results\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Low BCS\", \"High BCS\", \"BCS effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Low count (6)\", 0.372, 0.268, \"-0.104\"]\n          - [\"High count (22)\", 0.312, 0.178, \"-0.134\"]\n          - [\"Count effect\", \"-0.060\", \"-0.090\", \"interaction: -0.027\"]\n      - title: \"2×2 Type Confusion Rate\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Low BCS\", \"High BCS\", \"ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Low count (6)\", 0.008, 0.045, \"5.6x\"]\n          - [\"High count (22)\", 0.018, 0.072, \"4.0x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 2×2 interaction plot (F1) — 两条近似平行线，高 count 线略陡，显示微弱超加性\"\n      - \"Fig: 2×2 interaction plot (type confusion rate) — 交叉放大，high-count high-BCS 显著最高\"\n    analysis: >\n      2×2 结果核心支持 multi-channel 正交模型。BCS 主效应（F=22.8）大于 count 主效应（F=14.2），\n      说明在 Few-NERD 上 confusability 是更强的降级因子。交互效应 p=0.087 表明实质上加法模型足够，\n      轻微超加性可在论文中讨论但不改变核心叙事。这一结果直接支持 SDGD 的设计原理：\n      单独优化 batch 内 confusability（而非同时优化 count）已经足够捕获大部分可分解的性能损失。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-007: Error Taxonomy\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Systematic Error Taxonomy\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      在 exp-002 数据上系统分类 FP 错误为四类：type_substitution、boundary_error、\n      false_negative、hallucination，按 BCS quartile 分 bin 统计分布。\n    expected_results:\n      error_distribution_by_bcs_quartile:\n        Q1_low_bcs:\n          type_substitution_pct: 6.2\n          boundary_error_pct: 14.8\n          false_negative_pct: 58.3\n          hallucination_pct: 20.7\n          total_errors: 385\n        Q2:\n          type_substitution_pct: 12.5\n          boundary_error_pct: 13.2\n          false_negative_pct: 51.8\n          hallucination_pct: 22.5\n          total_errors: 412\n        Q3:\n          type_substitution_pct: 22.1\n          boundary_error_pct: 11.9\n          false_negative_pct: 44.6\n          hallucination_pct: 21.4\n          total_errors: 448\n        Q4_high_bcs:\n          type_substitution_pct: 38.4\n          boundary_error_pct: 10.5\n          false_negative_pct: 32.3\n          hallucination_pct: 18.8\n          total_errors: 521\n      monotonic_trends:\n        type_substitution_vs_bcs: \"单调递增 6.2→38.4%，Kendall τ=0.92\"\n        false_negative_vs_bcs: \"单调递减 58.3→32.3%，Kendall τ=-0.88\"\n        boundary_error_vs_bcs: \"微弱递减 14.8→10.5%，不显著\"\n        hallucination_vs_bcs: \"无趋势 20.7→18.8%，Kendall τ=-0.21\"\n      by_count_level:\n        count_6:\n          Q1_type_sub_pct: 4.8\n          Q4_type_sub_pct: 31.2\n          Q1_fn_pct: 61.5\n          Q4_fn_pct: 38.1\n        count_12:\n          Q1_type_sub_pct: 7.9\n          Q4_type_sub_pct: 44.7\n          Q1_fn_pct: 54.2\n          Q4_fn_pct: 27.8\n      chi_squared_bcs_vs_error_type:\n        statistic: 89.4\n        p: 1.2e-16\n        df: 9\n    result_rationale: >\n      Type substitution 与 BCS 强单调递增是 Claim 2 的核心机械证据：高 confusability batch 中，\n      模型正确识别了 entity span 但将其标注为语义邻近的错误类型。这是 confusability 通道的签名错误。\n      False negative 与 BCS 递减是因为在高 BCS batch 中，模型更倾向于\"猜错类型\"而非\"完全遗漏\"——\n      当多个相似类型在 prompt 中共现时，模型被激活去标注更多 span，但标注质量下降。\n      Hallucination 和 boundary error 与 BCS 无关，因为它们由其他因素驱动（幻觉=模型先验偏差，\n      边界=tokenization/span 识别问题），与类型相似度正交。\n      这一分解证实了 multi-channel 模型：count→omission(FN)，confusability→substitution。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Error Type Distribution by BCS Quartile (%)\"\n        columns: [\"BCS quartile\", \"Type sub.\", \"Boundary\", \"False neg.\", \"Halluc.\", \"Total\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Q1 (low)\", 6.2, 14.8, 58.3, 20.7, 385]\n          - [\"Q2\", 12.5, 13.2, 51.8, 22.5, 412]\n          - [\"Q3\", 22.1, 11.9, 44.6, 21.4, 448]\n          - [\"Q4 (high)\", 38.4, 10.5, 32.3, 18.8, 521]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: stacked bar chart — 四类错误按 BCS quartile 的占比变化，type_sub 从底部明显膨胀\"\n      - \"Fig: dual-axis plot — type_substitution rate (左轴, 递增) vs false_negative rate (右轴, 递减) 随 BCS quartile\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error taxonomy 是 Claim 2（multi-channel degradation）最直接的机械证据。\n      Type substitution 从 Q1 的 6.2% 飙升到 Q4 的 38.4%（6.2x），而 false negative 反向变化，\n      hallucination 稳定。这精确对应 multi-channel 模型的预测：confusability 通道选择性地增加\n      类型混淆错误，而非所有类型错误。count_12 条件下效应更强（Q4 type_sub=44.7%），\n      因为更多类型在 prompt 中同时出现时，confusability 的累积效应更大。\n      Chi-squared 高度显著（p=1.2e-16）确认 BCS quartile 与错误类型分布非独立。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-008: SDGD-zero on Few-NERD (R2)\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero Few-NERD (R2 revision)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-zero R2：修复 R1 的阈值和合并策略问题。基于 Qwen3 embedding pairwise SCS，\n      构建 confusability graph（阈值 τ=0.82），图着色分组，每组独立推理后合并。\n      对比 single-pass full-schema baseline。\n    expected_results:\n      r2_fixes:\n        threshold: \"τ=0.82 (R1 used 0.90, too aggressive → batches still confusable)\"\n        merge_strategy: \"span-level confidence dedup with type priority (R1 used naive union → duplicate spans)\"\n        batch_config: \"8 batches, avg 8.25 types/batch (range: 6-11)\"\n      sdgd_zero_results:\n        f1: 0.469\n        precision: 0.548\n        recall: 0.410\n        n_api_calls: 8\n        wall_clock_minutes: 12.5\n      single_pass_baseline:\n        f1: 0.414\n        precision: 0.648\n        recall: 0.304\n        n_api_calls: 1\n        wall_clock_minutes: 2.8\n      delta_vs_singlepass:\n        delta_f1_pp: 5.5\n        delta_recall_pp: 10.6\n        delta_precision_pp: -10.0\n        f1_p_value: 0.003\n        verdict: \"PASS — F1 显著提升，recall 大幅改善，precision 可控下降\"\n      per_batch_analysis:\n        mean_batch_bcs: 0.762\n        max_batch_bcs: 0.801\n        min_batch_bcs: 0.718\n        singlepass_bcs: 0.847\n        bcs_reduction_pct: 10.0\n      batch_level_breakdown:\n        batch_1: {n_types: 8, bcs: 0.738, f1: 0.385}\n        batch_2: {n_types: 9, bcs: 0.762, f1: 0.352}\n        batch_3: {n_types: 7, bcs: 0.721, f1: 0.401}\n        batch_4: {n_types: 11, bcs: 0.801, f1: 0.312}\n        batch_5: {n_types: 8, bcs: 0.745, f1: 0.378}\n        batch_6: {n_types: 9, bcs: 0.773, f1: 0.345}\n        batch_7: {n_types: 8, bcs: 0.752, f1: 0.368}\n        batch_8: {n_types: 6, bcs: 0.718, f1: 0.415}\n      type_confusion_rate:\n        sdgd_zero: 0.021\n        single_pass: 0.038\n        reduction_pct: 44.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      R1 失败的根因是两个实现问题：（1）SCS 阈值 τ=0.90 过高，导致 confusability graph 过于稀疏，\n      图着色产生的分组仍包含大量高相似度对（0.82-0.90 范围被遗漏）；\n      （2）naive union merge 在多个 batch 对同一 span 产生不同类型标注时直接取并集，\n      引入大量重复和矛盾预测。R2 将 τ 降至 0.82（基于 Few-NERD pairwise SCS 分布的 P90），\n      确保 top-10% 相似度对被强制分离；merge 策略改为 span-level confidence dedup，\n      当多个 batch 对同一 text span 产生不同类型时取置信度最高者。\n      F1 从 0.414 提升至 0.469（+5.5pp）主要来自 recall 改善（+10.6pp）：\n      较小的 batch（8 types vs 66 types）显著减少了 attention dilution，模型遗漏更少的 entity。\n      Precision 下降（-10.0pp）因为 8 个 batch 的合并引入了少量 spurious predictions，\n      但 confidence-based merge 将其控制在可接受范围。\n      净 F1 收益 +5.5pp 在 [3, 8] 范围中部，合理反映了 zero-shot 图着色方法的局限——\n      embedding 相似度只是 empirical confusability 的代理，最优分组需要 calibration data（→ exp-010）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"SDGD-zero R2 vs Single-pass on Few-NERD (66 types)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Precision\", \"Recall\", \"API calls\", \"Wall-clock (min)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass\", 0.414, 0.648, 0.304, 1, 2.8]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero R2\", 0.469, 0.548, 0.410, 8, 12.5]\n          - [\"Δ\", \"+5.5pp\", \"-10.0pp\", \"+10.6pp\", \"+7\", \"+9.7\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: F1/Precision/Recall bar chart — SDGD-zero vs single-pass，显示 F1 净提升来自 recall 的大幅改善\"\n      - \"Fig: per-batch BCS vs F1 scatter — 8 个 batch 内部，低 BCS batch 有更高 F1，验证 confusability-aware 分组的有效性\"\n      - \"Fig: merge 前后 prediction overlap 热力图 — 展示 confidence dedup 的效果\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-zero R2 的成功直接验证了 Claim 3：confusability-aware 分组本身有价值。\n      +5.5 F1 pp 中，约 2.2pp 来自 count reduction（见 exp-013），3.3pp 来自 confusability-aware grouping。\n      Per-batch 分析显示 batch 4（BCS=0.801, F1=0.312）vs batch 8（BCS=0.718, F1=0.415）\n      的对比直接体现了 SDGD 的内部一致性——即使在 SDGD 的优化分组内，\n      残余 confusability 差异仍然预测性能差异。\n      Type confusion rate 下降 44.7% 是机械证据：SDGD 通过分离 confusable pair 直接减少了 Channel 2 错误。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-009: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-zero 在 MAVEN 168 event types 上的 cross-task 验证。\n      基于 MiniLM embedding（MAVEN 上有效的 pairwise proxy），graph coloring 分组。\n    expected_results:\n      sdgd_zero_results:\n        relaxed_f1: 0.305\n        exact_f1: 0.022\n        n_batches: 14\n        avg_types_per_batch: 12.0\n        n_api_calls: 14\n        wall_clock_minutes: 22.4\n      single_pass_baseline:\n        relaxed_f1: 0.272\n        exact_f1: 0.014\n        n_api_calls: 1\n        wall_clock_minutes: 4.2\n      random_batching_baseline:\n        relaxed_f1: 0.282\n        n_api_calls: 14\n      delta_vs_singlepass:\n        delta_relaxed_f1_pp: 3.3\n        p_value: 0.012\n      delta_vs_random:\n        delta_relaxed_f1_pp: 2.3\n        p_value: 0.038\n      type_confusion_reduction:\n        sdgd_zero_rate: 0.035\n        single_pass_rate: 0.058\n        reduction_pct: 39.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 上 SDGD 收益（+3.3pp relaxed F1）小于 Few-NERD（+5.5pp），原因有二：\n      （1）MAVEN 的 SCS 分布更集中（mean=0.216, std=0.103），图着色的\"分离空间\"更小，\n      无法像 Few-NERD 那样找到明确的低相似度分组；\n      （2）MAVEN F1 与 count 正相关（exp-004），batch 缩小到 12 types 会损失部分 count-context 效益，\n      部分抵消了 confusability reduction 的收益。\n      使用 MiniLM 而非 Qwen3 是正确选择，因为 MiniLM pairwise 信号在 MAVEN 上有效（r=0.120）而 Qwen3 无效。\n      vs random 的 +2.3pp 确认 confusability-aware 分组在同质 schema 上仍然有价值，\n      尽管收益小于跨域 schema。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"SDGD-zero on MAVEN (168 types, MiniLM embedding)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Relaxed F1\", \"Exact F1\", \"API calls\", \"Δ relaxed F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass (168 types)\", 0.272, 0.014, 1, \"—\"]\n          - [\"Random batching (k=14)\", 0.282, 0.017, 14, \"+1.0pp\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero (k=14)\", 0.305, 0.022, 14, \"+3.3pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN 三方法对比 bar chart — 显示 SDGD > random > single-pass\"\n      - \"Fig: SDGD vs random per-batch scatter — SDGD batch 的 BCS 更低且方差更小\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 上的正向结果完成 SDGD 的 cross-task 验证（NER + ED），\n      证明 confusability-aware 分组在不同任务和 schema 特征下均有效。\n      效应量较小但仍然显著（p=0.012 vs single-pass），足以支持 Claim 3。\n      值得注意的是 embedding 选择的重要性——在 MAVEN 上使用 Qwen3 embedding 的 SDGD\n      可能无效（因为 Qwen3 pairwise 信号不显著），这强化了论文中\"task-appropriate embedding\"的建议。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-010: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal Few-NERD\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-cal：使用 5-10 calibration examples 构建经验 confusion matrix，\n      替代 embedding SCS 作为 confusability proxy，再用 graph coloring 分组。\n      对比 SDGD-zero。\n    expected_results:\n      calibration_cost:\n        n_calibration_examples: 8\n        n_calibration_api_calls: 8\n        calibration_wall_clock_minutes: 4.5\n      sdgd_cal_results:\n        f1: 0.488\n        precision: 0.556\n        recall: 0.435\n        n_api_calls: 9\n        wall_clock_minutes: 14.2\n        total_api_calls_incl_calibration: 17\n      sdgd_zero_comparison:\n        sdgd_zero_f1: 0.469\n        delta_f1_pp: 1.9\n        p_value: 0.042\n      calibration_vs_embedding_correlation:\n        empirical_vs_qwen3_scs_spearman: 0.58\n        empirical_vs_miniLM_scs_spearman: 0.43\n        verdict: \"经验 confusability 与 embedding proxy 中等相关，但经验版更准确\"\n      confusion_matrix_properties:\n        n_nonzero_pairs: 312\n        n_total_pairs: 2145\n        sparsity: 0.854\n        top_empirical_pair: \"person-other ↔ person-politician (confusion=23/8 examples)\"\n        top_embedding_pair: \"same pair (BCS=0.934)\"\n        agreement_top_20: \"85% overlap\"\n        disagreement_examples: \"building-library ↔ building-theater (high SCS=0.91, low empirical=0)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 高 1.9 F1 pp，因为经验 confusion matrix 直接捕获了\n      LLM 的实际混淆模式，而 embedding SCS 只是语义相似度的代理。\n      两者差距不大（1.9pp）因为 embedding proxy 已经相当好——top-20 confusable pairs 有 85% 重叠。\n      差异主要来自 edge cases：某些 embedding 上高相似但 LLM 实际不混淆的 pair\n      （如 building-library ↔ building-theater，LLM 依靠上下文线索有效区分），\n      以及 embedding 上不相似但 LLM 实际混淆的 pair（可能由于 training data 偏差）。\n      Calibration 的额外成本（8 API calls）使总 API calls 从 8 增至 17，\n      但仍远低于 per-type splitting（66 calls），且 F1 接近 per-type 水平。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"SDGD Variant Comparison on Few-NERD\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"P\", \"R\", \"API calls (total)\", \"Δ F1 vs single-pass\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass\", 0.414, 0.648, 0.304, 1, \"—\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero\", 0.469, 0.548, 0.410, 8, \"+5.5pp\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-cal\", 0.488, 0.556, 0.435, 17, \"+7.4pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: empirical confusion matrix heatmap (top-30 types) — 可视化实际混淆模式\"\n      - \"Fig: SCS vs empirical confusion scatter — r=0.58，验证 embedding proxy 的合理性和局限性\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-cal 的 +1.9pp 增量验证了 SDGD 框架的可扩展性——更好的 confusability 估计\n      直接转化为更好的分组和更高的 F1。这也为 SDGD-zero 的实用性提供了参照：\n      在无 calibration data 的冷启动场景下，SDGD-zero 已能获得大部分收益（5.5/7.4 = 74%），\n      calibration 的边际收益递减。论文中 SDGD-zero 作为默认推荐，SDGD-cal 作为高精度选项。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-011: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      SDGD-cal 在 MAVEN 168 types 上的完整对比。\n      使用 MiniLM embedding 和 10 calibration examples。\n    expected_results:\n      sdgd_cal_results:\n        relaxed_f1: 0.318\n        exact_f1: 0.025\n        n_api_calls: 14\n        total_api_calls_incl_calibration: 24\n      full_comparison_table:\n        single_pass: {relaxed_f1: 0.272, api_calls: 1}\n        random_k14: {relaxed_f1: 0.282, api_calls: 14}\n        sdgd_zero_miniLM: {relaxed_f1: 0.305, api_calls: 14}\n        sdgd_cal: {relaxed_f1: 0.318, api_calls: 24}\n        per_type: {relaxed_f1: 0.325, api_calls: 168}\n      delta_sdgd_cal_vs_zero: \"+1.3pp\"\n      delta_sdgd_cal_vs_singlepass: \"+4.6pp\"\n      calibration_improvement_on_maven:\n        empirical_vs_miniLM_spearman: 0.49\n        verdict: \"经验混淆信号在同质 schema 上增量更大，因为 embedding 信号更弱（MiniLM r=0.120）\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 上 SDGD-cal vs SDGD-zero 的增量（1.3pp）与 Few-NERD 的（1.9pp）相近，\n      因为 calibration data 在同质 schema 上的价值更高——MiniLM embedding 在 MAVEN 上\n      虽然 pairwise 信号显著但效应较弱（r=0.120 vs Few-NERD Qwen3 r=0.156），\n      经验数据能更精确地识别实际高混淆对。\n      SDGD-cal（0.318）接近 per-type splitting（0.325）但 API calls 少 7x（24 vs 168），\n      完成 SDGD 框架在效率/质量 tradeoff 上的定位。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Full Comparison Table: MAVEN (168 types)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Relaxed F1\", \"API calls\", \"Δ vs single-pass\", \"Latency ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass\", 0.272, 1, \"—\", \"1.0x\"]\n          - [\"Random (k=14)\", 0.282, 14, \"+1.0pp\", \"5.3x\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero (MiniLM)\", 0.305, 14, \"+3.3pp\", \"5.3x\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-cal\", 0.318, 24, \"+4.6pp\", \"8.5x\"]\n          - [\"Per-type (k=168)\", 0.325, 168, \"+5.3pp\", \"40.0x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN full method comparison — F1 vs API calls Pareto plot，SDGD-cal 位于 Pareto 前沿\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 完整对比表是论文 Table 3（或 4）的核心内容。SDGD-cal 在 Pareto 前沿上\n      明确优于 random 和 single-pass，接近 per-type 但成本大幅降低。\n      这完成了 Claim 3 的全部证据链：confusability-aware 分组在两个任务上均有效，\n      且 SDGD 框架提供了从 zero-shot 到 calibrated 的灵活选项。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-012: Multi-model (LLaMA-3.3-70B)\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Multi-model Validation (LLaMA-3.3-70B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: >\n      用 LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct 在 Few-NERD 上复现 exp-002 协议：\n      count curve + extreme/random batch + pairwise/per-type 分析。\n    expected_results:\n      count_curve:\n        count_1: {f1: 0.298, recall: 0.612, precision: 0.198}\n        count_6: {f1: 0.275, recall: 0.445, precision: 0.200}\n        count_12: {f1: 0.318, recall: 0.312, precision: 0.324}\n        count_22: {f1: 0.282, recall: 0.258, precision: 0.311}\n        count_44: {f1: 0.405, recall: 0.370, precision: 0.447}\n        count_64: {f1: 0.378, recall: 0.288, precision: 0.548}\n      pairwise_analysis:\n        qwen3_embedding:\n          n_pairs: 1953\n          pearson_r: 0.138\n          pearson_p: 3.2e-9\n          spearman_rho: 0.144\n          spearman_p: 8.1e-10\n          nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.228\n          nonzero_spearman_p: 5.7e-5\n        miniLM_embedding:\n          pearson_r: 0.072\n          pearson_p: 0.0015\n      per_type_analysis:\n        n_types: 60\n        filter: \"freq>=5\"\n        qwen3_spearman_rho: -0.265\n        qwen3_spearman_p: 0.041\n        miniLM_spearman_rho: -0.058\n        miniLM_spearman_p: 0.66\n      extreme_batch:\n        count_6_high_bcs_f1: 0.195\n        count_6_low_bcs_f1: 0.342\n        count_12_high_bcs_f1: 0.215\n        count_12_low_bcs_f1: 0.398\n        confusion_rate_ratio_count6: 18.5\n        confusion_rate_ratio_count12: 12.3\n      cross_model_comparison:\n        qwen3_pairwise_r: 0.156\n        llama_pairwise_r: 0.138\n        delta: -0.018\n        both_significant: true\n        fisher_z_test_p: 0.52\n        verdict: \"效应量无显著差异，two models 一致\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA-3.3-70B 的 pairwise r=0.138 略低于 Qwen3 的 0.156，因为不同模型的\n      confusability 敏感度略有差异——LLaMA 的指令遵从能力更强（70B 参数 + Instruct 调优），\n      可能在部分高 confusability pair 上仍能正确区分。但差异不显著（Fisher z p=0.52），\n      确认 confusability signal 是跨模型稳定的现象。\n      Per-type ρ=-0.265（p=0.041）方向和显著性与 Qwen3（ρ=-0.293, p=0.020）一致，\n      说明 Few-NERD 的跨域 schema 结构使 per-type 信号在不同提取模型上均稳定。\n      Extreme batch confusion rate ratio 12-18x 与 Qwen3 的 10-28x 范围一致。\n      LLaMA 整体 F1 略低于 Qwen3（count_64: 0.378 vs 0.414），可能因为 LLaMA 的\n      NER 提示模板适配度稍差，但不影响 confusability 信号的相对模式。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-model Pairwise Comparison on Few-NERD\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Embedding\", \"Pearson r\", \"p-value\", \"Spearman ρ\", \"p-value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"Qwen3\", 0.156, \"4.6e-12\", 0.160, \"1.3e-12\"]\n          - [\"LLaMA-3.3-70B\", \"Qwen3\", 0.138, \"3.2e-9\", 0.144, \"8.1e-10\"]\n          - [\"Fisher z-test\", \"—\", \"Δ=0.018\", \"p=0.52\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n      - title: \"Cross-model Extreme Batch Confusion Rate\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Count\", \"High-BCS rate\", \"Low-BCS rate\", \"Ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", 6, 0.0728, 0.0014, \"27.5x\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", 12, 0.0480, 0.0061, \"9.9x\"]\n          - [\"LLaMA-70B\", 6, 0.0612, 0.0033, \"18.5x\"]\n          - [\"LLaMA-70B\", 12, 0.0445, 0.0036, \"12.3x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 双模型 pairwise scatter overlay — Qwen3 (蓝) vs LLaMA (橙)，回归线斜率接近\"\n      - \"Fig: cross-model confusion rate ratio comparison — 两模型一致的 high/low BCS 差异模式\"\n    analysis: >\n      Multi-model 验证完成 cross_model_significant: 2/2 的要求。两个差异显著的架构\n      （Qwen3-32B decoder vs LLaMA-3.3-70B decoder）在 pairwise confusability signal、\n      per-type direction、extreme batch effect 上全部一致，排除了单模型 artifact 的可能性。\n      Fisher z-test 的 p=0.52 确认两模型效应量无统计差异。\n      这是对 reviewer concern \"only one model\" 的完整回应。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-013: Random Batching Ablation\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Random Batching Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      与 SDGD-zero 相同的 k=8 batch count，但 batch composition 完全随机。\n      5 次随机种子取平均。隔离 confusability-aware grouping 的贡献。\n    expected_results:\n      random_batching_results:\n        mean_f1: 0.436\n        std_f1: 0.012\n        mean_precision: 0.530\n        mean_recall: 0.370\n        n_api_calls: 8\n        n_random_seeds: 5\n      comparison:\n        single_pass_f1: 0.414\n        sdgd_zero_f1: 0.469\n        random_f1: 0.436\n        delta_random_vs_singlepass: \"+2.2pp\"\n        delta_sdgd_vs_random: \"+3.3pp\"\n        delta_sdgd_vs_singlepass: \"+5.5pp\"\n      decomposition:\n        count_reduction_contribution: \"2.2pp (40% of total SDGD gain)\"\n        confusability_aware_contribution: \"3.3pp (60% of total SDGD gain)\"\n      random_batch_bcs_stats:\n        mean_batch_bcs: 0.838\n        std_batch_bcs: 0.025\n        sdgd_mean_batch_bcs: 0.762\n        bcs_reduction_by_sdgd: \"9.1%\"\n      type_confusion_rates:\n        random: 0.031\n        sdgd_zero: 0.021\n        single_pass: 0.038\n    result_rationale: >\n      Random batching 获得 +2.2pp 改善（vs single-pass）完全来自 count reduction：\n      从 66 types/batch 降到 ~8 types/batch 减少了 attention dilution，提升了 recall。\n      但 random batch 的 mean BCS（0.838）接近 single-pass（0.847），\n      因为随机分组不会系统性地分离 confusable pair。\n      SDGD-zero 的额外 +3.3pp 来自 confusability-aware grouping：mean batch BCS 降至 0.762，\n      type confusion rate 从 0.031 降至 0.021（32% 减少）。\n      60%/40% 的贡献分解表明 confusability-aware grouping 是 SDGD 价值的主要来源，\n      而非简单的 batch count reduction。这是 Claim 3 最关键的证据——\n      SDGD 优于 random batching（same k）直接证明了 confusability-aware 分组的独立价值。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Ablation: SDGD-zero vs Random Batching vs Single-pass\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Recall\", \"Type confusion rate\", \"Mean batch BCS\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass (k=1)\", 0.414, 0.304, 0.038, 0.847]\n          - [\"Random (k=8)\", 0.436, 0.370, 0.031, 0.838]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero (k=8)\", 0.469, 0.410, 0.021, 0.762]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: F1 gain decomposition waterfall chart — single-pass → +2.2pp (count) → +3.3pp (confusability) → SDGD\"\n      - \"Fig: 5 random seeds 的 F1 分布 + SDGD-zero 的位置（显著高于随机分布上界）\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是论文中最重要的 ablation。SDGD vs random（same k）的 +3.3pp gap（p < 0.01）\n      是 Claim 3 的充分必要证据——confusability-aware 分组本身有价值，\n      SDGD 的收益不仅仅来自简单的 schema 分解。\n      5 次随机种子的 std=0.012 表明 random batching 的方差较小，SDGD-zero 的 0.469\n      显著高于随机分布的上界（0.436 + 2×0.012 = 0.460），排除了 lucky draw 的可能性。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-014: Per-type Splitting (UniNER-style)\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Per-type Splitting Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      每个类型单独一个 batch（k=66），每次只提取一种类型。\n      UniNER-style 的上界实验。对比 SDGD 和 single-pass。\n    expected_results:\n      per_type_results:\n        f1: 0.475\n        precision: 0.512\n        recall: 0.443\n        n_api_calls: 66\n        wall_clock_minutes: 68.5\n      comparison:\n        single_pass: {f1: 0.414, api_calls: 1, wall_clock: 2.8}\n        random_k8: {f1: 0.436, api_calls: 8, wall_clock: 12.5}\n        sdgd_zero: {f1: 0.469, api_calls: 8, wall_clock: 12.5}\n        sdgd_cal: {f1: 0.488, api_calls: 17, wall_clock: 14.2}\n        per_type: {f1: 0.475, api_calls: 66, wall_clock: 68.5}\n      sdgd_zero_vs_per_type:\n        f1_gap: \"-0.6pp\"\n        api_calls_ratio: \"8.25x fewer\"\n        wall_clock_ratio: \"5.5x faster\"\n        verdict: \"SDGD-zero 达到 per-type 的 98.7% F1，但成本仅 12%\"\n      sdgd_cal_vs_per_type:\n        f1_gap: \"+1.3pp (SDGD-cal 更高)\"\n        api_calls_ratio: \"3.9x fewer\"\n        verdict: \"SDGD-cal 超过 per-type，因为保留了部分 cross-type 上下文\"\n      per_type_error_analysis:\n        type_confusion_rate: 0.002\n        false_negative_rate: 0.31\n        hallucination_rate: 0.28\n        boundary_error_rate: 0.16\n        note: \"type confusion 几乎消除，但 hallucination 上升——单类型 prompt 缺乏跨类型约束\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-type splitting 几乎消除了 type confusion（rate=0.002 vs single-pass 0.038），\n      验证了 confusability 是可通过分组解决的。但 F1 只有 0.475，低于预期的\"上界\"，\n      因为存在两个反向效应：\n      （1）缺乏 cross-type context：当只有一个类型时，模型无法利用\"这个 span 更像 X 而非 Y\"的对比信息，\n      导致某些模糊 span 被遗漏或被 hallucinate（hallucination rate 上升至 0.28）；\n      （2）recall 上升到 0.443（最高），因为 attention 完全集中在单一类型上。\n      SDGD-zero（0.469）接近 per-type（0.475）的原因是：SDGD 的 8-type batch 保留了\n      有限但有用的 cross-type context，同时移除了大部分 confusability。\n      SDGD-cal（0.488）超过 per-type（0.475）是关键发现——证明 optimal decomposition\n      不是\"最大分解\"而是\"最优 confusability/context tradeoff\"，SDGD 框架正好在此定位。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Full Method Comparison on Few-NERD (66 types)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"P\", \"R\", \"API calls\", \"Wall-clock\", \"Efficiency\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Single-pass\", 0.414, 0.648, 0.304, 1, \"2.8 min\", \"baseline\"]\n          - [\"Random (k=8)\", 0.436, 0.530, 0.370, 8, \"12.5 min\", \"+2.2pp / 8 calls\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-zero (k=8)\", 0.469, 0.548, 0.410, 8, \"12.5 min\", \"+5.5pp / 8 calls\"]\n          - [\"Per-type (k=66)\", 0.475, 0.512, 0.443, 66, \"68.5 min\", \"+6.1pp / 66 calls\"]\n          - [\"SDGD-cal (k=9)\", 0.488, 0.556, 0.435, 17, \"14.2 min\", \"+7.4pp / 17 calls\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: F1 vs API calls Pareto plot — SDGD-zero 和 SDGD-cal 在 Pareto 前沿，per-type 被 dominated\"\n      - \"Fig: error type composition comparison — per-type 消除 type_sub 但增加 hallucination\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-type 实验揭示了一个反直觉的结果：最大分解≠最优分解。\n      SDGD-cal 超过 per-type 因为保留了 cross-type context 带来的消歧能力。\n      这使论文的 method 贡献更强——SDGD 不仅仅是\"把类型分开\"的简单策略，\n      而是在 confusability reduction 和 context preservation 之间的 principled tradeoff，\n      graph coloring 框架正好 operationalize 了这个 tradeoff。\n      Pareto plot 是论文的核心 figure 之一：清晰展示 SDGD variants 在效率/质量空间的优势。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-015: SCS Validation\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SCS Proxy Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-015\"\n    description: >\n      用 exp-010 的经验 confusion matrix 作为 ground truth，验证 embedding SCS\n      作为 confusability proxy 的排序准确性。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen3_scs_vs_empirical:\n        spearman_rho: 0.584\n        spearman_p: 2.3e-18\n        kendall_tau: 0.421\n        kendall_p: 8.1e-15\n        top_20_overlap: 0.85\n        top_50_overlap: 0.72\n      miniLM_scs_vs_empirical:\n        spearman_rho: 0.432\n        spearman_p: 1.7e-10\n        kendall_tau: 0.312\n        kendall_p: 3.4e-8\n        top_20_overlap: 0.65\n        top_50_overlap: 0.54\n      precision_at_k:\n        qwen3_p_at_10: 0.90\n        qwen3_p_at_20: 0.85\n        qwen3_p_at_50: 0.72\n        miniLM_p_at_10: 0.70\n        miniLM_p_at_20: 0.65\n        miniLM_p_at_50: 0.54\n      failure_modes:\n        false_positive_scs: \"embedding 高相似但不混淆：通常是共享 supertype 但 subtype 名称足够区分\"\n        false_negative_scs: \"embedding 低相似但实际混淆：通常因共现频率或 prompt 位置效应\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen3 SCS 与经验 confusability 的 Spearman ρ=0.584 表明 embedding 是合理但非完美的代理。\n      相关性显著但不为 1 的原因：\n      （1）embedding 相似度捕获语义距离，而实际 confusion 还受 prompt 位置、类型名称字面相似性、\n      训练数据频率等非语义因素影响；\n      （2）Qwen3 embedding 来自指令调优后的最后一层，保留了较多任务相关信息，因此优于 MiniLM。\n      Top-20 的 85% 重叠解释了为什么 SDGD-zero 已经很有效——最 confusable 的 pair 大多被正确识别。\n      SDGD-cal 的增量主要来自修正那 15% 的错误排序。\n      Precision@k 在 top-10 最高（0.90），说明 embedding proxy 在识别\"最危险\"pair 时最可靠。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"SCS Proxy Validation\"\n        columns: [\"Embedding\", \"Spearman ρ\", \"Kendall τ\", \"Top-20 overlap\", \"P@10\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3\", 0.584, 0.421, \"85%\", 0.90]\n          - [\"MiniLM\", 0.432, 0.312, \"65%\", 0.70]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: SCS vs empirical confusion scatter (Qwen3) with Precision@k curve inset\"\n      - \"Fig: failure mode examples — 标注 FP (高 SCS 低 confusion) 和 FN (低 SCS 高 confusion) 的具体 pair\"\n    analysis: >\n      SCS validation 完成了 SDGD 框架的理论闭环：embedding SCS 是合理的 confusability proxy\n      （ρ=0.58），但经验数据更好（SDGD-cal > SDGD-zero）。\n      论文的实用建议：cold-start 用 SDGD-zero（Qwen3 embedding），\n      有少量 calibration data 后切换到 SDGD-cal。Qwen3 明显优于 MiniLM 作为 proxy\n      在 Few-NERD 上，但 MAVEN 上反转（→ 使用 task-appropriate embedding）。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5b7ad92b-97f6-47f3-a0ef-2ecf2be282d0","total_cost_usd":0.7450379999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17638,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":24647,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17638,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":24647,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17638,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17638},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":12595,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.012695,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":24647,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":17638,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7323429999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"74239a2e-80e6-4a6e-95d2-404e8ff88739"}
